{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars","id":1294421,"title":"How does the Wild Hunt ever Corner Lunars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-06T09:04:10-08:00","id":1294421,"title":"How does the Wild Hunt ever Corner Lunars?","content":"Seriously how does the Wild Hunt ever Corner a Lunar they can\u2019t Ambush? Unless the Lunar specifically wants to make a Last stand they have the option of turning into a Bird and Flying away, or turning into a fish and swimming away, or turning into a badgermole and digging deep deep down. So how do they corner Lunars the same way they Corner Solars? Will we get something like Sidereal Magic\u2019s to explain this? Should I have just put this in the ask devs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:10:47-08:00","id":1294422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars#post1294421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously how does the Wild Hunt ever Corner a Lunar they can\u2019t Ambush? Unless the Lunar specifically wants to make a Last stand they have the option of turning into a Bird and Flying away, or turning into a fish and swimming away, or turning into a badgermole and digging deep deep down. So how do they corner Lunars the same way they Corner Solars? Will we get something like Sidereal Magic\u2019s to explain this? Should I have just put this in the ask devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it\u2019s a reasonable ask deva question. Though you may be underestimating Dragon Blooded and Sidereals, especially their archers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:19:26-08:00","id":1294424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294422#post1294422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it\u2019s a reasonable ask deva question. Though you may be underestimating Dragon Blooded and Sidereals, especially their archers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is why I said unless it\u2019s an ambush. But even in an ambush a murder of crows flies off and they are going to murder each crow?<br /> <br /> But if not in an ambush all they have to do is fly away from the Wyld Hunt, like that simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:23:26-08:00","id":1294428,"title":"","content":"Not every Lunar has the right Heart's Blood to escape? Capturing someone important to them or threatening something they care about so they don't want to run? Faking weakness so the Lunar decides to commit and doesn't realise they should have run until it's too late?<br /> <br /> Lunars sure do have a lot of ways to escape Wyld Hunts, but there's a bunch of ways to force or trick a Lunar into engaging, and of course a lot of Lunars do get away, but with only 400 Lunars around tops, even a few kills is a pretty significant dent in the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:44:47-08:00","id":1294432,"title":"","content":"If they're anything like <b>my </b>players, they don't run away when they see a fight coming, even if they're grossly outnumbered. They just start fighting, supremely confident that they can win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T09:48:00-08:00","id":1294435,"title":"","content":"You don't attack the lunar, you attack the lunar's <i>home.</i> You come for their friends. You turn their family against them. You make the lunar confront you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:03:20-08:00","id":1294441,"title":"","content":"Although Lunars are one of the only character types in the game who actually can become perfectly spherical, this still doesn't make them perfectly spherical frictionless rational actors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":27}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:06:28-08:00","id":1294442,"title":"","content":"If I may quote myself elsewhere:<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levie, post: 22435127, member: 55610</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having thought more on the subject of Lunars versus Wyld Hunts, one dynamic I envisioned was the idea that one thing that experienced shahan-yas try to drill into their students is a paraphrase of Robert DeNiro's ethos in Heat: never become too attached to something you can't abandon at a moment's notice.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levie, post: 22435127, member: 55610</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appended with elaborations like not getting hung up on the idea of sunk costs, not letting things like pride or anger cloud their judgement, don't get too hung up on pursuing a weakened foe if there's too much risk of dying; better to turn into a sparrow and flee now and return to complete your operation later.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And a persistent bane to the Silver Pact is that their members are not perfectly rational actors; even after centuries, there's always a chance that somebody might become a bit too attached to a protectorate, a bit too fixated on the idea that they've invested too much to accept things having gone south quickly, a bit too hateful of whom they're fighting. They can let the fight become a slugging match, and that can often be very dangerous for them when surrounded by hostile Exalted.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Plus occasions where simple fallibility just results in a miscalculation; the ideal operation lasts long enough to draw a Wyld Hunt that will invest in chasing you, and cuts and runs (preferably to a trap or an ambush) before they can draw a net around you. That can be tenuous; the golden window is probably often narrow, and judging the ideal moment to try and draw them into a chase might be a bit up in the air.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And lest this seem to weight Dragon Blooded successes on Lunar failings, all of this can go double for when the assault comes from Exalted who are especially good or canny; they mobilise more quickly than a Lunar might have expected, they're strong and smart enough to make a Lunar's ambush too dangerous for them, they deliberately engage in actions intended to draw the Lunar out or back. It's a complex interplay.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Really, the best Wyld Hunts probably have the people and resources to attack from multiple directions; anticipate the Lunar's most likely path of retreat, put somebody there ahead of time, catch them between a hammer and anvil.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:09:15-08:00","id":1294445,"title":"","content":"Plus, while turning into an animal can make it harder to attack, Dragon Blooded can still shoot down birds. It's conceivable, depending on how fast or wounded the Lunar is when they take that step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars#post1294421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">turning into a badgermole and digging deep deep down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Burrower Merit is going to let them Scrooge McDuckit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:10:38-08:00","id":1294447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294424#post1294424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that is why I said unless it\u2019s an ambush. But even in an ambush a murder of crows flies off and they are going to murder each crow?<br /> <br /> But if not in an ambush all they have to do is fly away from the Wyld Hunt, like that simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this happening right in front of them? Because for the typical Lunar they need to take a miscellaneous action to become a bird then attempt to re-establish surprise next round by using the crows as cover. If that's successful, they're going to start killing the crows. It looks simple on paper, but escaping like this is going to be potentially rather harrowing if you've got multiple Dragon-Blooded shooting at you from the outset and then annihilating your cover as you try to get away. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:16:15-08:00","id":1294450,"title":"","content":"There's also a question of how, if it's done as a fight is ending, it might be easy to pick out the crow that is glowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:27:17-08:00","id":1294451,"title":"","content":"Those do all sound like good stunts for a withdraw roll though, of which you have to complete three of.<br /> <br /> Edit; and imagine getting shot down while trying to run. Better to die on your feet then live on your knees kinda sums up at least part of the Lunar rage spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 03-06-2019, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:42:24-08:00","id":1294452,"title":"","content":"I'd wager the most common way is attacking something the lunar will feel compelled to stay and defend. Especially young lunars who have yet to get a handle on the rage burning away inside them as their version of essence fever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:29:03-08:00","id":1294477,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, possibly the best help Sidereals might be able to give is information. Information about the general area the Lunar is in. Information about where their passions lie. Information about the secrets they hold. And so on. (I\u2019m expecting the 3e version of the Sids Google-Spider to be really, really nice.)<br /> <br /> All of which should help a Wyld Hunt manage to force the issue instead of wandering around lost in the woods, running into shrubbery, trying to find a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:26:37-08:00","id":1294495,"title":"","content":"So again it sounds like they have to one Ambush a Lunar, which is so insanely easier said then done since Lunars don\u2019t usually have an address registered at the local post office, and they are as likely to say have a home on a cliff side or an underwater Manse as they are to just live in a tree or a house. It\u2019s much harder to sneak up a whole Wyld Hunt Team then it is to sneak a single Exalt. And considering Wyld Hunts stack in their favor by trying to get ten Exalts per Anthema and some mortal support troops, that\u2019s mighty hard to sneak into a small space.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or two goad a Lunar into initiating Last Stand Procedures.<br /> <br /> So most likely Lunars will know about the Shikari before the Hunt directly senses them.<br /> <br /> And you don\u2019t automatically sense Lunars are Lunars in a big forest full of Animals. A Lunar might not even rest in Human form. And unless you are right on the Lunar, or the Lunar is glowing, if they are say taking cover from arrow fire behind a tree or a Bush how are they not paranoid trying kill all the Crows flying away or boats running away, meanwhile the Lunar could have turned into a tick or a vole.<br /> <br /> And if they kill every living thing and burn down the forest they don\u2019t really know they even killed the Lunar. Meanwhile if they spend attention sniping every bird (which honestly only The Exalts can be relied upon to do) you are also revealing your local if you are a sniper, and also distracting yourself in the middle of Battle. The Wyld Hunt doesn\u2019t have the benefit of being players at the table, well unless they do, they don\u2019t know what going on all the time hunting slippery Pete.<br /> <br /> And all this is taking into account they accurately gauged the number of Anathema, if they are having tea with another Lunar, or a God Friend or Hell a Pack of Exalts the Sidereal is the one who needs to initiate escape protocols.<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunts are expensive and Lunars are slippery. If you expecting two Anathema or more now you are bringing 20 Dragon Blooded and an Army of you want more of a sure thing, less and you are gambling.<br /> <br /> And Lunars usually seem to be secret individuals, so at best you are targeting a whole culture or region that favors them and hoping they care enough to defend genocide. Or maybe a Sidereal sneaks info on more specific loved ones.<br /> <br /> And genociding whole cultures is how you develop leagues forming against the Realm, it\u2019s also expensive and doesn\u2019t have much glory if you don\u2019t succeed, so you better start slaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:32:22-08:00","id":1294498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294445#post1294445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, while turning into an animal can make it harder to attack, Dragon Blooded can still shoot down birds. It's conceivable, depending on how fast or wounded the Lunar is when they take that step.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think the Burrower Merit is going to let them Scrooge McDuckit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already covered the bird situation, you either kill every bird and be distracted or you let them get away. And even if you shoot every bird it\u2019s only a fighting chance you shoot them down, they can make a turn into the trees, flying down a cliff, hide in a tree, or swim in a river<br /> <br /> <br /> And unless you flood the ground why wouldn\u2019t a Lunar turn into a groundhog/gopher and enter the already existing network of tunnels in their lair.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar isn\u2019t glowing you essentially need the best Exalted trackers around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:32:55-08:00","id":1294499,"title":"","content":"It's almost like Wyld Hunts are incredible drains on resources and aren't designed to actually be cost effective but instead about maintaining and concentrating power, and were mostly supported by the Empress, and they basically stopped as soon as the houses became more interested in sniping at each other then worrying about the barbarians outside their doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:38:49-08:00","id":1294500,"title":"","content":"I see inducing plagues and Wyld Hunts as the most solid method of draining the realms coffers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:41:09-08:00","id":1294501,"title":"","content":"If you can constantly trigger Wyld Hunts then get away without dying then yes, you are winning the long war, because you are one person pulling an army and a bunch of highly trained people away from their jobs for no benefit to them.<br /> <br /> This is providing they don't find out who you are, what culture you came from, and who your parents are and respond by burning your village down to the ground to attempt to draw you out or something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T13:57:32-08:00","id":1294505,"title":"","content":"At this point it seems we're talking about a single Lunar doing nothing of consequence in the middle of nowhere. What's to be gained from sending them to their next incarnation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T14:05:27-08:00","id":1294506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294424#post1294424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that is why I said unless it\u2019s an ambush. But even in an ambush a murder of crows flies off and they are going to murder each crow?<br /> <br /> But if not in an ambush all they have to do is fly away from the Wyld Hunt, like that simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Lunar is old and powerful enough to turn into a murder of crows, the Wyld Hunt already fucked up a while ago. There\u2019s a reason they prioritize the newly Exalted over hunting down the Old Guard of the Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T14:35:57-08:00","id":1294510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294506#post1294506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar is old and powerful enough to turn into a murder of crows, the Wyld Hunt already fucked up a while ago. There\u2019s a reason they prioritize the newly Exalted over hunting down the Old Guard of the Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, nobody is sending a Hunt after Leviathan. Well, maybe if you wanted to get rid of some political enemies and could somehow force them to go. <br /> <br /> There's ways to chase down birds though, DBs can fly, shoot area of effect attacks, dragon vortex, that kind of thing. They can swim fast too, tear up the earth Toph style. Or just keep a Lunar pinned with Unbreakable Facination Kata or Hungry Earth Stike or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T14:58:57-08:00","id":1294514,"title":"","content":"Nah, they totally still send them after elders. The preview on Ma-Ha-Suchi's domain mentions that he has had multiple Wyld Hunts sent after him despite being a powerful and well entrenched first age elder (some of them even manage to actually make it to his doorstep and required him to personally dispatch them). No true Prince of the Earth is going to cower in the face of a vile Anathema just because previous generations screwed the pooch and didn't kill it before it could reach its full potential in blasphemous power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T14:59:59-08:00","id":1294515,"title":"","content":"This seems pretty academic. How do they corner a Lunar they aren't actively engaging? They goad it into battle by threatening something the lunar refuses to abandon.<br /> <br /> How do they keep attacking once battle has started? They give chase, and succeed on rush actions. Being a bird or fish or super-badger doesn't obviate the need to make the dice rolls to disengage, and ut's pretty difficult to actually escape from battle once joined.<br /> <br /> It does mean that if you're out to kill a Lunar ut's imperative you confront them on your terms; but that's par for the course with any Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T15:02:20-08:00","id":1294516,"title":"","content":"Although Ma Ha Suchi's lair's writeup does mention hunts getting to his front door.<br /> <br /> And then dying horribly, presumably.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aaaaand that got mentioned while I was typing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-06-2019, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:00:49-08:00","id":1294523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294498#post1294498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already covered the bird situation, you either kill every bird and be distracted or you let them get away. And even if you shoot every bird it\u2019s only a fighting chance you shoot them down, they can make a turn into the trees, flying down a cliff, hide in a tree, or swim in a river</div> </div> </div> </div>You are saying this in response to my point about how turning into a bird won't do a damn thing about your anima, without in any way addressing it<br /> <br /> Don't shoot all of the birds, <i>shoot the one that is glowing</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And unless you flood the ground why wouldn\u2019t a Lunar turn into a groundhog/gopher and enter the already existing network of tunnels in their lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're shifting the goalposts away from a statement of a utility for escape in every possible situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Lunar isn\u2019t glowing</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they probably left before the fight got very serious.<br /> <br /> Your parameters for what constitutes an ambush seem sufficiently broad that I don't understand why you have a problem with them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you're describing capabilities that are just the basic framework for why the setting is the way it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:39:06-08:00","id":1294532,"title":"","content":"Not him but can't you fix the glowing problem by using charms that eat up your anima? Pretty sure they even have a charm that would let them stick a different bird with their anima banner in the process.<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, looked it up and that charm has some pretty steep setup needed to pawn it off on something else. Its also essence 3 (and manipulation 5) and so a custom charm making it easier to give it to someone else would probably be essence 4 or 5 and significant stat investment in being a trickster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 03-06-2019, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:43:07-08:00","id":1294534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars#post1294421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously how does the Wild Hunt ever Corner a Lunar they can\u2019t Ambush? Unless the Lunar specifically wants to make a Last stand they have the option of turning into a Bird and Flying away, or turning into a fish and swimming away, or turning into a badgermole and digging deep deep down. So how do they corner Lunars the same way they Corner Solars? Will we get something like Sidereal Magic\u2019s to explain this? Should I have just put this in the ask devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember, Dynasts have been training to deal with problems like this since they've been children, and some have the experience of centuries behind them.<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't impossible to detect. They have tells and animas (&amp; they keep injuries/amputations when shapeshifting), and most of them aren't sitting around in a cave hiding all the time. They have essence fever like any other exalt. They're driven to do heroic and stupid stuff, and not all of them are as cautious about keeping a low profile as they could be. So, almost all Lunars, especially young and inexperienced ones, are leaving some trail of evidence.<br /> Dragon-bloods can track Lunars using transhuman abilities in investigation, awareness. survival and stealth. Survival in particular can be used to detect unusual behaviour of animals. They use teams of hunting animals, some of them supernatural. They use the help of spiritual allies, who can dematerialize and use Measure the Wind to scan the nature of wads of creatures at once. They can disguise themselves as regular mortals not from the Realm, live in an area for months, gain the locals' trust, meet the local Lunar, have a festive round of drinks at the local tavern, and slit his throat in his sleep.<br /> <br /> A dragon-blood with decent stats &amp; an athletics excellency can outrun a cheetah, outdig a badger, and leap and catch a hummingbird flying above his head, so animal forms aren't a perfect getaway. And if a dragon-blood did get in close range, it's unlikely any of those creatures could disengage; it's hard to turn your back on someone who's about to shove a sword in it!. And if they can't disengage immediately, those dragonbloods are going to attempt to grapple (Dragonbloods can grapple at range with their charms like a water bender, btw), and then you can't even disengage. And Lunars are at a disadvantage, since they can't shapeshift into an animal form reflexively without the right charm; they have to disengage at a flurry penalty if they want to fly away. And Lunars can't use those animal's abilities to their full extent unless they have decent physical stats (Many Lunars will have them, but not all of them). Furthermore, they can't fly or dig if they're cornered in an enclosed space like a building. They can't fly away easily if a sorcerer has used Beckoning that which stirs the sky to create a hurricane, and they can't dig if one uses Raising the Earth's Bones to disrupt their tunnelling network.<br /> <br /> Flight? A dragon-blood can fly with an athletics charm at Essence 3, or they can chase flying Lunars with trained flying mounts, spells like storm windrider, flying summoned minions like Azata, flying spiritual allies like storm serpents, a squadron of hackmen mercenaries, artifact wings, etc. Hunting Lunars is one of the top priorities of a multi-continent spanning empire of unimaginable wealth; they have the resources for exotic stuff like this. They can also ground flying foes with the use of bolas, lassoes, barbed javelins tied to a rope, that aforementioned waterbender charm, etc.<br /> <br /> Burrowing? How safe is it to burrow near an Earth Aspect's bonfire anima? You can try to follow vibrations/sound with an awareness excellency, and there's charms that let Dragon-bloods do that perfectly. Anything in a tunnel can be mashed to a bloody pulp if a feat of strength or a smashing attack with a goremaul hits the ground above and collapses the tunnel system. I bet Shikari just love when Lunars do something like this. Otherwise, allied or summoned earth elementals or the right demons can potentially phase through earth, and trained hunting animals (Immaculate stoat squad!) of the right size can follow through small tunnels.<br /> <br /> Water Aspects can move in water without penalty. They don't even need to be fit to outswim slower fish.<br /> <br /> And also, sorcery and artifacts. Lots of 'em. Whole libraries of spells and panoplies of artifacts which have been developed to solve these very problems for well over a millennia, even since the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> And you can imagine that this is all the more deadly when you add Sidereals, astrology, and their heavenly allies into the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-06-2019, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:46:47-08:00","id":1294535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294532#post1294532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not him but can't you fix the glowing problem by using charms that eat up your anima? Pretty sure they even have a charm that would let them stick a different bird with their anima banner in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an essence 4 manipulation charm that has 9 prerequisites, I believe.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, the one or two Lunars extant who actually know that charm, likely a century or two old, will be damn hard bastards to find and kill.<br /> <br /> We're talking &quot;Wyld Hunt vs. Lunars&quot;, not the &quot;Wyld Hunt vs. the sneakiest damn Lunars it is possible to construct using the best charms&quot;, because obviously plenty of Lunars do live and grow old despite the best efforts of the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-06-2019, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:55:13-08:00","id":1294538,"title":"","content":"Yeah, had forgotten how much of an investment getting it was when I made that suggestion. Honestly, anyone that devoted to being a trickster probably isn't going to get ambushed in the first place unless its part of some convoluted scheme to fake their death or something. And I guess if they get 'ambushed' on purpose it no longer counts as an ambush anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T17:31:55-08:00","id":1294545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294424#post1294424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even in an ambush a murder of crows flies off and they are going to murder each crow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how a murder of crows would probably be represented with a battle group (if they were participating in the combat) or trivial opponents (if they weren't), it wouldn't be unreasonable for a Dragon-Blooded to fire a Death of Obsidian Butterflies into the mass and expect to wipe out all but one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T18:22:59-08:00","id":1294553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294506#post1294506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar is old and powerful enough to turn into a murder of crows, the Wyld Hunt already fucked up a while ago. There\u2019s a reason they prioritize the newly Exalted over hunting down the Old Guard of the Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not what I\u2019m talking about. I\u2019m talking about a Lunar using a normal murder of crows. Unless they Lunar is famous for specific tricks the Wyld Hunt can\u2019t assume the Lunar can or can\u2019t turn into one Crow or a murder.<br /> <br /> So many Lunar Tricks I can see flat out working unless the Wyld Hunt genocides all life in a ten mile radius so there isn\u2019t cover. Hell a Lunar could turn into a horse and throw a beheaded Shikari and treetrunk onto itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T18:43:15-08:00","id":1294556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294553#post1294553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s not what I\u2019m talking about. I\u2019m talking about a Lunar using a normal murder of crows. Unless they Lunar is famous for specific tricks the Wyld Hunt can\u2019t assume the Lunar can or can\u2019t turn into one Crow or a murder.<br /> <br /> So many Lunar Tricks I can see flat out working unless the Wyld Hunt genocides all life in a ten mile radius so there isn\u2019t cover. Hell a Lunar could turn into a horse and throw a beheaded Shikari and treetrunk onto itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning into a murder of crows is an Essence 5 charm with 6 prerequisites. Remember, according to the core, &quot;Essence 5 is a mark of extreme prowess, vanishingly rare among the ranks of the comparatively short-lived Dragon-Blooded and noteworthy even among centuries-old elder Celestial Exalted.&quot; The Silver Pact is at constant war (or, at least, the wyld hunt is at constant war against them), and there can't be too many who live to be centuries old. Not all of them are Essence 5, and certainly not all Essence 5 Lunars have this charm. Pretty much every Essence 5 charm may be a unique charm for one elder exalt at any one point in history. There is no &quot;normal murder of crows&quot; charm, and a Lunar who can turn into crows isn't &quot;famous for specific tricks&quot;, they're the sort of primordial god-monster who could potentially make behemoths squeal in terror and flee, and slaughter an entire army in single combat.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there are no lunars living today who know this charm. Perhaps one does, and hasn't used it against Dragon-bloods in centuries. Perhaps several wyld hunts have encountered this charm, but there have never been any survivors. This may be a mythical ability, and the realm's experts in lunar combat might have no idea if it truly exists.<br /> <br /> Now, for an elder Lunar like this, and not knowing what the hell they may be capable, destroying all life in a ten mile radius is a reasonable tactic for the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> What other tricks were you thinking of? Were any of them less than Essence 5?<br /> <br /> I'm thoroughly enjoying this thread btw, thank you for starting it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","user":"Slarn!","date":". 03-06-2019, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:31:57-08:00","id":1294567,"title":"","content":"So first and foremost, remember target one for a Wyld Hunt is a new Lunar ideally before they've gotten any training. Doesn't matter if between shapeshifting, sorcery, and necromancy a Lunar could become literally impossible to pin down;* a new Lunar doesn't know most of their own tricks and can't apply them as well. So you hunt the new bloods first since you catch them before anyone's explained and well the guy turned into a mammoth, but if that's all they can do that's not too much of a problem compared to worrying about the dude seagulling it to the ocean or a river and fleeing at the speed of angry fish. Also remember no plan is 100%, your best odds of killing a Lunar involve finding them while they're asleep and decapitating them, barring that amount of great fortune one has to accept a bit more chance.<br /> <br /> So sorcery is also a fun trick to employ for countering lunars. The devil maw creates a glorious suction of all water in an area around it, so smaller escape animals are potentially dying like mad ,if you're lucky one turns back into a lunar, and if it tries to burrow out then you conveniently have a lot of liquid to flood their escape hole with. This is also not counting demons or elementals that might be able to track and hunt the lunar in other ways. <br /> <br /> Now your primary tactic is gonna be overwhelming force and surprise. Not just ambushes just stuff they didn't expect. Remember a Lunar isn't necessarily going to cut and run as soon as there are signs of a Hunt. After all killing, crippling, and/or maiming all the members is going to be a moral damager not counting any and all resources as a result of those individuals.Of course this means actually having to engage the Wyld Hunt and if they aren't expecting it getting caught by someone casting Mists of the Eventide is gonna be rough and the Lunar wouldn't have been able to plan for that if they didn't know, the Hunt could have. Overwhelming force is what it sounds like, a shapeshifting bug out plan doesn't help much if you've got a half a dozen people on you at that exact moment to strike at your new beast form, or just have to contend with a mixture of DB anima banners in full force. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Exageration for the sake of making a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:36:53-08:00","id":1294568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294556#post1294556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turning into a murder of crows is an Essence 5 charm with 6 prerequisites. Remember, according to the core, &quot;Essence 5 is a mark of extreme prowess, vanishingly rare among the ranks of the comparatively short-lived Dragon-Blooded and noteworthy even among centuries-old elder Celestial Exalted.&quot; The Silver Pact is at constant war (or, at least, the wyld hunt is at constant war against them), and there can't be too many who live to be centuries old. Not all of them are Essence 5, and certainly not all Essence 5 Lunars have this charm. Pretty much every Essence 5 charm may be a unique charm for one elder exalt at any one point in history. There is no &quot;normal murder of crows&quot; charm, and a Lunar who can turn into crows isn't &quot;famous for specific tricks&quot;, they're the sort of primordial god-monster who could potentially make behemoths squeal in terror and flee, and slaughter an entire army in single combat.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there are no lunars living today who know this charm. Perhaps one does, and hasn't used it against Dragon-bloods in centuries. Perhaps several wyld hunts have encountered this charm, but there have never been any survivors. This may be a mythical ability, and the realm's experts in lunar combat might have no idea if it truly exists.<br /> <br /> Now, for an elder Lunar like this, and not knowing what the hell they may be capable, destroying all life in a ten mile radius is a reasonable tactic for the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> What other tricks were you thinking of? Were any of them less than Essence 5?<br /> <br /> I'm thoroughly enjoying this thread btw, thank you for starting it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure they are asking what happens if a lunar tries to blend in with a regular murder of crows not created by charms or sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:39:20-08:00","id":1294569,"title":"","content":"What's a devil maw? Elemental or spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:41:25-08:00","id":1294570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294569#post1294569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a devil maw? Elemental or spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell. You create a mouth on your hand that drinks all the water in the vicinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:51:03-08:00","id":1294571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294570#post1294570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell. You create a mouth on your hand that drinks all the water in the vicinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohmygod so cool. <br /> <br /> .... I don't want to buy an entire book just for the spells in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:51:39-08:00","id":1294572,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and if we're talking about Lunars bringing out Essence 5 charms, maybe the Wyld Hunt brought along somebody who knows Dragon Vortex Attack. Normally I'd say no way, but if the Hunt is actually going after one of those Essence 5 monsters then maybe. If you contribute 5 unique elements to it that's like a difficulty 9 environmental hazard with at least a range of Long, and probably more into one or two of the Extreme Long bands, and a damage of, well, kills you basically. It's not a totally inescapable attack, it takes a lot to pull off and if the Lunar can make a difficulty 9 resistance roll then she escapes it with no issue, but it's also not totally impotent.<br /> <br /> At least unless Lunars have a charm to perfectly negate environmental damage, which is theoretically possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:06:01-08:00","id":1294574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294568#post1294568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure they are asking what happens if a lunar tries to blend in with a regular murder of crows not created by charms or sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. Couldn't you just use a read intentions action in that case against the whole mass of crows to see which one's faking, at a heavy penalty?<br /> <br /> One of the previewed chapter fiction is relevant: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/lunars-fangs-at-the-gate-for-exalted-3rd-ed/posts/2425777\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2425777</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:09:57-08:00","id":1294575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294571#post1294571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ohmygod so cool.<br /> <br /> .... I don't want to buy an entire book just for the spells in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to, though if you want to look at the night thief tier on the Lunar Kickstarter to get it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Though yeah sorcerery is probably a big asset in Wyld Hunts just because not counting workings you can spring all kinds of weird stuff on an unsuspecting target. Lunar tries to attack the night guards for the Hunt or a high priority target and gets caught by the random torches suddenly being revealed as the recepticles of the Virtuous Guardian of Flame spell. If you can get it figured out I would totally have a special arrow or the like holding a suspended cast of Flight of the Brilliant Raptor* for Lunars trying escape via horse or some other form of extremely fast animal form.<br /> <br /> And of course there's messing with the enviorment, I mean if you're expecting a blizzard and the Lunar isn't That Which Stirs the Sky gives you an edge and the Lunar makes the mistake that the sudden severe weather will stop the Hunt while the Hunt was planning for that since they got to the area.<br /> <br /> *This would probably be expensive as all get out and the spell containing projectile would probably be bloody obvious as an abnormal round, but it would be cool and probably useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:51:57-08:00","id":1294579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294523#post1294523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are saying this in response to my point about how turning into a bird won't do a damn thing about your anima, without in any way addressing it<br /> <br /> Don't shoot all of the birds, <i>shoot the one that is glowing</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're shifting the goalposts away from a statement of a utility for escape in every possible situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then they probably left before the fight got very serious.<br /> <br /> Your parameters for what constitutes an ambush seem sufficiently broad that I don't understand why you have a problem with them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you're describing capabilities that are just the basic framework for why the setting is the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming you aren\u2019t trying to hide when you are already a literal miles high silver beacon. I\u2019m assuming if you are a silver Beacon you already chose to initiate the whole last stand protocol. <br /> <br /> Where did I imply you would be glowing? If you are glowing you only can expect to outrace them or make more then an hour obstacle between you and the enemy like going to the other side of Springfield Gorge.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not shifting the goalpost. Heavy woodlands, savanas and even swamps have already existing animal burrows, the biggest thing keeping other animals out is they are usually too small for predators and animals like rodents feel they have a disadvantage in the homes of rival, a Lunar Gopher is going to be something another Gopher is not goin to find worth fighting. Of course you are not going to turn to a gopher on a boat or a tree. And even if there isn\u2019t other tunnels. Why isn\u2019t it an option to sneak under a log and burrow? Unless they smoke you out what are they going to do turn into a snake and go after you? They need to have specific powers to id that it\u2019s you there, and then they can shake the ground, that is not a gaurantee they will find you. And that is what I\u2019m saying they would be leaving before they really got into the thick of things.<br /> <br /> And that last paragraph means little to nothing. Whenever you hit a crossroad where one option is to speak with clarity and the other option is to sacrifice clarity for ominousness or some perceived cool points you try to go that route. It works with the writers, but with you it can often lead to miscommunication.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m poking the setting with a stick mate, I\u2019m not crapping on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:52:16-08:00","id":1294580,"title":"","content":"That which stirs the sky? Weather control? By how much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:53:53-08:00","id":1294581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294505#post1294505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point it seems we're talking about a single Lunar doing nothing of consequence in the middle of nowhere. What's to be gained from sending them to their next incarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we? Where do you get that? And besides technically it\u2019s their religious duty to hunt the Anathema where they dwell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:07:54-08:00","id":1294583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294510#post1294510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, nobody is sending a Hunt after Leviathan. Well, maybe if you wanted to get rid of some political enemies and could somehow force them to go. <br /> <br /> There's ways to chase down birds though, DBs can fly, shoot area of effect attacks, dragon vortex, that kind of thing. They can swim fast too, tear up the earth Toph style. Or just keep a Lunar pinned with Unbreakable Facination Kata or Hungry Earth Stike or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s another thing unless you have a whole Wyld Hunt Composed of Deep Sea Navy Seals, or specific magical items it\u2019s not practical to go after any Lunar who makes their home in the Sea Much less Leviathan.<br /> <br /> I know theirs ways to chase down birds, but unless you keep an eye on the Lunar the whole time you can easily loose track of them. And even if you spot them, there is no gaurantee you are getting them, and if you loose them unless they want to challenge you a Lunar can go to ground anywhere in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:09:57-08:00","id":1294584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294506#post1294506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar is old and powerful enough to turn into a murder of crows, the Wyld Hunt already fucked up a while ago. There\u2019s a reason they prioritize the newly Exalted over hunting down the Old Guard of the Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I\u2019m saying they could be just one of the crows, or even giving the impression they could one of the Crows or maybe one of the bees from the two beehives knocked over, or maybe a boar from that family of hogs scurry out of the bush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:11:57-08:00","id":1294585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294580#post1294580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That which stirs the sky? Weather control? By how much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the area's normal weather and what you're hoping to get out of it. Can't do natural disaster level weather, so no hurricanes; tornadoes; or cyclones; but you can still whip up pretty heavy weather if you can get the successes. How hard that is will vary based on what you're hoping to achieve and how hard it goes against the normal weather for the area and time of year. So trying to get a light shower in a rainny season for an area not that hard; torrential downpour the same season will be harder due to more intense, but still easier than trying to get a decent rain in the middle of the summer in Gem.<br /> <br /> Oh another fun method, give the Lunar a reason not to run. Like we've mentioned attacking something the Lunar doesn't want to lose, but there's also the option of being something the Lunar doesn't want to continue existing. A lot of Lunars are going to have reasons to hate the Realm and pretty much any followers of the Immaculate Order resulting in any Lunar failing to control their rage getting stuck in due to just trying to hard to kill the Hunt because that's what they are. I mean just saying you want to draw Leviathan into the open and make sure he's not running let him find out you've got the remains of his former mate and have converted the skull into a codpiece, he's probably not leaving until everyone involved is so very dead.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Chosen of Battles Warning: Lunar getting stuck into the battle and commiting to victory or death may not be conducive to a long life span for you and your army. Angry Lunar vengeance may be contagious along alliances and bloodlines. Please consult your hearthmates before instigating berserk Lunar fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:21:17-08:00","id":1294588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294534#post1294534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just remember, Dynasts have been training to deal with problems like this since they've been children, and some have the experience of centuries behind them.<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't impossible to detect. They have tells and animas (&amp; they keep injuries/amputations when shapeshifting), and most of them aren't sitting around in a cave hiding all the time. They have essence fever like any other exalt. They're driven to do heroic and stupid stuff, and not all of them are as cautious about keeping a low profile as they could be. So, almost all Lunars, especially young and inexperienced ones, are leaving some trail of evidence.<br /> Dragon-bloods can track Lunars using transhuman abilities in investigation, awareness. survival and stealth. Survival in particular can be used to detect unusual behaviour of animals. They use teams of hunting animals, some of them supernatural. They use the help of spiritual allies, who can dematerialize and use Measure the Wind to scan the nature of wads of creatures at once. They can disguise themselves as regular mortals not from the Realm, live in an area for months, gain the locals' trust, meet the local Lunar, have a festive round of drinks at the local tavern, and slit his throat in his sleep.<br /> <br /> A dragon-blood with decent stats &amp; an athletics excellency can outrun a cheetah, outdig a badger, and leap and catch a hummingbird flying above his head, so animal forms aren't a perfect getaway. And if a dragon-blood did get in close range, it's unlikely any of those creatures could disengage; it's hard to turn your back on someone who's about to shove a sword in it!. And if they can't disengage immediately, those dragonbloods are going to attempt to grapple (Dragonbloods can grapple at range with their charms like a water bender, btw), and then you can't even disengage. And Lunars are at a disadvantage, since they can't shapeshift into an animal form reflexively without the right charm; they have to disengage at a flurry penalty if they want to fly away. And Lunars can't use those animal's abilities to their full extent unless they have decent physical stats (Many Lunars will have them, but not all of them). Furthermore, they can't fly or dig if they're cornered in an enclosed space like a building. They can't fly away easily if a sorcerer has used Beckoning that which stirs the sky to create a hurricane, and they can't dig if one uses Raising the Earth's Bones to disrupt their tunnelling network.<br /> <br /> Flight? A dragon-blood can fly with an athletics charm at Essence 3, or they can chase flying Lunars with trained flying mounts, spells like storm windrider, flying summoned minions like Azata, flying spiritual allies like storm serpents, a squadron of hackmen mercenaries, artifact wings, etc. Hunting Lunars is one of the top priorities of a multi-continent spanning empire of unimaginable wealth; they have the resources for exotic stuff like this. They can also ground flying foes with the use of bolas, lassoes, barbed javelins tied to a rope, that aforementioned waterbender charm, etc.<br /> <br /> Burrowing? How safe is it to burrow near an Earth Aspect's bonfire anima? You can try to follow vibrations/sound with an awareness excellency, and there's charms that let Dragon-bloods do that perfectly. Anything in a tunnel can be mashed to a bloody pulp if a feat of strength or a smashing attack with a goremaul hits the ground above and collapses the tunnel system. I bet Shikari just love when Lunars do something like this. Otherwise, allied or summoned earth elementals or the right demons can potentially phase through earth, and trained hunting animals (Immaculate stoat squad!) of the right size can follow through small tunnels.<br /> <br /> Water Aspects can move in water without penalty. They don't even need to be fit to outswim slower fish.<br /> <br /> And also, sorcery and artifacts. Lots of 'em. Whole libraries of spells and panoplies of artifacts which have been developed to solve these very problems for well over a millennia, even since the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> And you can imagine that this is all the more deadly when you add Sidereals, astrology, and their heavenly allies into the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d like to point out Lunars are just as likely to have spirit allies as the Wyld Hunt, and if Hunted to their home turf they probably have the home field advantage with friendly spirit neighbors tipping them off before they are cornered. And Burrowing is a tactic that they can be assumed to be doing when they aren\u2019t, that means covering all means of escape at once, and if you have Dragonblooded tracking one avenue of escape that means they aren\u2019t tracking others. To cover all their bases they need to have a definite eye on the Lunar every second or they need to annihilate all living creatures within several miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:26:43-08:00","id":1294591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294545#post1294545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how a murder of crows would probably be represented with a battle group (if they were participating in the combat) or trivial opponents (if they weren't), it wouldn't be unreasonable for a Dragon-Blooded to fire a Death of Obsidian Butterflies into the mass and expect to wipe out all but one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that is a good tactic, but if it takes you even a couple turns and the murder is too diffused to wipe them out with one spell, not to mention you aren\u2019t a battle group when you are a bunch of animals fleeing otherwise what is the point of routing. And trivial opponents are not an auto kill when they are bird flying away, more like it\u2019s an auto kill to shoot a pirates Parrot or stab someone\u2019s dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:39:45-08:00","id":1294595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294556#post1294556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turning into a murder of crows is an Essence 5 charm with 6 prerequisites. Remember, according to the core, &quot;Essence 5 is a mark of extreme prowess, vanishingly rare among the ranks of the comparatively short-lived Dragon-Blooded and noteworthy even among centuries-old elder Celestial Exalted.&quot; The Silver Pact is at constant war (or, at least, the wyld hunt is at constant war against them), and there can't be too many who live to be centuries old. Not all of them are Essence 5, and certainly not all Essence 5 Lunars have this charm. Pretty much every Essence 5 charm may be a unique charm for one elder exalt at any one point in history. There is no &quot;normal murder of crows&quot; charm, and a Lunar who can turn into crows isn't &quot;famous for specific tricks&quot;, they're the sort of primordial god-monster who could potentially make behemoths squeal in terror and flee, and slaughter an entire army in single combat.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there are no lunars living today who know this charm. Perhaps one does, and hasn't used it against Dragon-bloods in centuries. Perhaps several wyld hunts have encountered this charm, but there have never been any survivors. This may be a mythical ability, and the realm's experts in lunar combat might have no idea if it truly exists.<br /> <br /> Now, for an elder Lunar like this, and not knowing what the hell they may be capable, destroying all life in a ten mile radius is a reasonable tactic for the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> What other tricks were you thinking of? Were any of them less than Essence 5?<br /> <br /> I'm thoroughly enjoying this thread btw, thank you for starting it!</div> </div> </div> </div>You are misreading my response when I say a normal murder of crows I don\u2019t mean a charm, I mean you take cover behind a tree or some bushes when the crows or whatever animals freak out and flee in a swarm ( crows, ravens, larks, butterflies, bees, you name it) if you lost sight of the Lunar that means you don\u2019t know it\u2019s not one of a thousand animals cheesing it in all directions. Just wake up one morning and run at a bush filled with thrushes or skylarks, they swarm out of the bush all wildly nilly. And unless you know it\u2019s a new Lunar you have no idea how mighty or old it is, Lunars do have a lot of centuries old elders, likely more then Sidereals but less then Dragonblooded but most aren\u2019t going to be essence five. But only someone like an experienced Sidereal advisor would know the ins and outs of Celestial powers anyways. Otherwise what Wyld Hunts underestimate every Elder Exalt and they die because they don\u2019t know half of their charms or capabilities. They only need to assume the whole Murder is one entity if they act that way anyways.<br /> <br /> Just think how Batman acts when out numbered. He riles up normal bats with hypersonics, and uses misdirection so the police or gangsters are firing at Shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":". 03-07-2019, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:03:59-08:00","id":1294600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294595#post1294595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are misreading my response when I say a normal murder of crows I don\u2019t mean a charm, I mean you take cover behind a tree or some bushes when the crows or whatever animals freak out and flee in a swarm ( crows, ravens, larks, butterflies, bees, you name it) if you lost sight of the Lunar that means you don\u2019t know it\u2019s not one of a thousand animals cheesing it in all directions. Just wake up one morning and run at a bush filled with thrushes or skylarks, they swarm out of the bush all wildly nilly. And unless you know it\u2019s a new Lunar you have no idea how mighty or old it is, Lunars do have a lot of centuries old elders, likely more then Sidereals but less then Dragonblooded but most aren\u2019t going to be essence five. But only someone like an experienced Sidereal advisor would know the ins and outs of Celestial powers anyways. Otherwise what Wyld Hunts underestimate every Elder Exalt and they die because they don\u2019t know half of their charms or capabilities. They only need to assume the whole Murder is one entity if they act that way anyways.<br /> <br /> Just think how Batman acts when out numbered. He riles up normal bats with hypersonics, and uses misdirection so the police or gangsters are firing at Shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't help when facing someone who's invested in awareness. They'll still be able to spot you from a mile away once they've spotted your tell. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:05:27-08:00","id":1294603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294588#post1294588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d like to point out Lunars are just as likely to have spirit allies as the Wyld Hunt, and if Hunted to their home turf they probably have the home field advantage with friendly spirit neighbors tipping them off before they are cornered. And Burrowing is a tactic that they can be assumed to be doing when they aren\u2019t, that means covering all means of escape at once, and if you have Dragonblooded tracking one avenue of escape that means they aren\u2019t tracking others. To cover all their bases they need to have a definite eye on the Lunar every second or they need to annihilate all living creatures within several miles.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294588#post1294588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you take cover behind a tree or some bushes when the crows or whatever animals freak out and flee in a swarm ( crows, ravens, larks, butterflies, bees, you name it) if you lost sight of the Lunar that means you don\u2019t know it\u2019s not one of a thousand animals cheesing it in all directions. Just wake up one morning and run at a bush filled with thrushes or skylarks, they swarm out of the bush all wildly nilly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think it comes down to having beefy stats and charms in stealth, so the lunars don't see you coming, awareness &amp; survival so you never, ever lose track of the Lunar, and investigation, so you can pick up the trace again if you fail. But you're right, dragon-blooded must lose lunars all the time this way, unless they plan well, and catch the Lunar at a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> Btw, Wildfire Taming Technique seems like it was made for this. It can be used to track a quarry magically with no need of physical spoor, which is perfect for shapeshifting prey. It can also burn down a whole forest killing all the animals for miles around and trap the lunar while the dragon-bloods hunt through it without being harmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:09:15-08:00","id":1294604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294591#post1294591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is a good tactic, but if it takes you even a couple turns and the murder is too diffused to wipe them out with one spell, ,,,</div> </div> </div> </div>An Essence 3 DB sorcerer in Earth Aura has very good odds of firing off DoOB between their Occult Excellency, the Heptagram bonuses, and DB Sorcery upgrade Charms. Given the range of DoOB... I'm not thinking &quot;Lunar hides in a group of animals&quot; is really that effective. Certainly not reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:11:12-08:00","id":1294605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294583#post1294583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s another thing unless you have a whole Wyld Hunt Composed of Deep Sea Navy Seals, or specific magical items it\u2019s not practical to go after any Lunar who makes their home in the Sea Much less Leviathan.<br /> <br /> I know theirs ways to chase down birds, but unless you keep an eye on the Lunar the whole time you can easily loose track of them. And even if you spot them, there is no gaurantee you are getting them, and if you loose them unless they want to challenge you a Lunar can go to ground anywhere in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, of course it's easy to lose track of them, but Dragonblooded are still exalts. We don't similarly have a problem with a Solar's perfect eyes being able to track a single bird through the trees, a DB shouldn't be that much worse at it. She's still got a super human ability to do so. You've even got charms like Sense Riding Technique so if you escape, they can still find you. For most people the idea of chasing a monkey through the treetops is absurd, but for a Wood Aspect with Graceful Dryad Dance they can actually do it better than a monkey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:18:04-08:00","id":1294607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294605#post1294605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That\u2019s another thing unless you have a whole Wyld Hunt Composed of Deep Sea Navy Seals, or specific magical items it\u2019s not practical to go after any Lunar who makes their home in the Sea Much less Leviathan.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't a group of water-aspects hop in a tidemare and a few elemental buddies and hunt underwater without difficulty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:29:48-08:00","id":1294608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294604#post1294604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Essence 3 DB sorcerer in Earth Aura has very good odds of firing off DoOB between their Occult Excellency, the Heptagram bonuses, and DB Sorcery upgrade Charms. Given the range of DoOB... I'm not thinking &amp;quot;Lunar hides in a group of animals&amp;quot; is really that effective. Certainly not reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. What about rapid firing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:31:41-08:00","id":1294609,"title":"","content":"There's a whole bunch of answers to this.<br /> <br /> 1. The Wyld Hunt <i>does</i> prefer to ambush Lunars, partially, no doubt, for this exact reason.<br /> <br /> 2. The Wyld Hunt is well-acquainted with what Lunars can do. If they're hunting you, and they know you can turn into a bird, they're gonna bring a bunch of skilled archers. If they're not sure they can corner you, they're going to rely on powerful poisons, sorcerous curses, and other magical effects that can kill you after the battle even if you escape, or at least leave you vulnerable as they hunt you down.<br /> <br /> 3. The Wyld Hunt prefers to fight Anathema when they're young (and, in the case of Lunars, this means when they have few forms.) Lunars who can survive to build a decent heart's blood library are likely to survive a while longer.<br /> <br /> 4. Most Lunars don't just want to run and hide all the time. They have things they want to accomplish, which causes them to put their neck out from time to time. Sometimes this results in their head getting cut off before they can slip away.<br /> <br /> 5. Experienced Lunars probably, actually, survive plenty of their encounters with the Wyld Hunt. The situations you're describing - Lunar turns into a bird or a mouse and slips off to fight another day - is very likely the default. Hunting Lunar Anathema is doubtless frustrating, and a Lunar who gets past the &quot;how do I shoot web&quot; stage likely escapes death many times after that. If they're aggressive and combat-oriented, I'm sure it's not uncommon for them to kill several DBs before they're finally corned and killed - Anathema are feared for a reason. Unfortunately for those Lunars, the DBs outnumber them far more than &quot;several&quot; times, and can afford to keep coming. Eventually, they screw up and die. Not all of them - a few have managed to live a very long time - but the ones that have lived the longest have generally carved out save havens so they don't have to constantly risk their lives. Because the DBs can afford to keep doing this over and over, and they only have to get lucky once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:36:36-08:00","id":1294610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294600#post1294600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't help when facing someone who's invested in awareness. They'll still be able to spot you from a mile away once they've spotted your tell. </div> </div> </div> </div>If they know your tell that is, and even an Awareness specialized Dragonblooded isn\u2019t super god tier for something like this like an Awarness Supernal Solar is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:39:09-08:00","id":1294612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294610#post1294610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they know your tell that is, and even an Awareness specialized Dragonblooded isn\u2019t super god tier for something like this like an Awarness Supernal Solar is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent stats and an excellency is more than good enough in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:40:14-08:00","id":1294613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294610#post1294610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they know your tell that is, and even an Awareness specialized Dragonblooded isn\u2019t super god tier for something like this like an Awarness Supernal Solar is.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... What? I know its supposed to be hard for heroic mortals, but DBs have excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:48:31-08:00","id":1294614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294607#post1294607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't a group of water-aspects hop in a tidemare and a few elemental buddies and hunt underwater without difficulty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they can, but that means they must form a very specialized Wyld Hunt, without an overwhelming mortal support, and with need for supernatural support specifically, and if they get ganked, very possible because well Lunars could easily have their own tidemares, and Vodnik, and Beastmen and 2nd Circle Demons who can ambush you, you loose a lot of very specialized individuals, meaning the next water safari is consider a bigger risk with less talent to tap. And even if you survive, well pretty much all Wyld Hunts I recall mentioned in the book that survive without winning seem to be depressed or disillusioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also catching New Solars is much more viable, if a worse time in the Realms History, then catching new Lunars. Even if the Lunars don\u2019t Exalt in the rim of the known world, which means a huge amount of time to discover it, prepare a hunt and go a hunting, they still have a lot of Lunar and Lunar allies beings on the look out for them, compared to Solars.<br /> <br /> But Hell I was always of the opinion the Silver Pact should have been keeping an eye out for New Solars to at least give some sort of offer too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:57:29-08:00","id":1294615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294613#post1294613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... What? I know its supposed to be hard for heroic mortals, but DBs have excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are also Exalts though. It\u2019s one thing to pick out a single bee amidst a hive, or a bird among a flock, that is assuming you know what to look for and Darkness isn\u2019t an issue, but Lunars are Also Exalts. They are Celestial Exalts with environmental and shape advantages. I\u2019d imagine considering the significant evasion advantage of a tiny form you would get a comparable stealth advantage, especially when you are tiny and more then medium range away in the dark. Excellencies is one thing but you are going to want more sureity then that. So far I see it just as conceivable stealthy tiny things in the dark amidsts thousands of similar shapes could be spotted but far from a sure thing considering this is another Exalt, one a tier above terrestrial.<br /> <br /> And Hell if the Lunar has a familiar all the more Batman Ninja options available to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:04:21-08:00","id":1294617,"title":"","content":"Tips for Wyld Hunting Lunars<br /> <br /> 1. When the Astrologers tell you of the appearance of a new Anathema, make haste. The Ogres amongst the Anathema use their profane magics to learn of these new Moon Mad and send forth their minions to capture them, so it is imperative to get there quickly.<br /> <br /> 2. Knowledge is key. All Silver Anathema have an identifying mark upon their bodies that cannot be altered, the Tell, so it is paramount to watch for this, but do not discount any other information that can be gleaned. The demon often retains the memories and some of the relationships held by their host body for a time after possession. These ties can be used to lure out the Anathema from their lair, to determine their likely habits and strategies, and what goals they might initially pursue. However, be forewarned. The warping that occurs when the demon takes a new host is most severe in the Silver Anathema, such that the final demon may not retain anything of the original host, not in body, mind, or soul. <br /> <br /> 3. Nearly every Wyld Hunt that has pursued a Silver Anathema has lost it at one point or another. Do not think of this as failure, but as another opportunity to learn. Most young Moon Mad instinctively know to steal the form of a bird or fish as soon as they can, but most only gain one form. When they change, watch their new form as much as you can, both to learn its markings and to see their Tell. This will help you to take them down a second time.<br /> <br /> 4. Practice hunting. Learn to track, hunt, and kill every animal under the sun, so that you cannot be surprised later. Learn the habits of animals, such that you may spot them acting strangely or flush them out depriving the Anathema of their concealment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:35:05-08:00","id":1294620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294615#post1294615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars are also Exalts though. It\u2019s one thing to pick out a single bee amidst a hive, or a bird among a flock, that is assuming you know what to look for and Darkness isn\u2019t an issue, but Lunars are Also Exalts. They are Celestial Exalts with environmental and shape advantages. I\u2019d imagine considering the significant evasion advantage of a tiny form you would get a comparable stealth advantage, especially when you are tiny and more then medium range away in the dark. Excellencies is one thing but you are going to want more sureity then that. So far I see it just as conceivable stealthy tiny things in the dark amidsts thousands of similar shapes could be spotted but far from a sure thing considering this is another Exalt, one a tier above terrestrial.<br /> <br /> And Hell if the Lunar has a familiar all the more Batman Ninja options available to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The advantage from being tiny is whoever is trying to spot you loses 2 successes. Everything else you are describing is circumstantial, and benefits non lunars just as much as lunars.<br /> <br /> If the lunar is not invested in dexterity and stealth then they are definitely at risk of being spotted by a dragonblooded who is invested in awareness. Especially if you consider the escalating penalties of -3/-4/-5 if you are attempting to go to ground, or just the -3 penalty for attempting stealth in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:35:35-08:00","id":1294621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294617#post1294617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tips for Wyld Hunting Lunars<br /> <br /> 1. When the Astrologers tell you of the appearance of a new Anathema, make haste. The Ogres amongst the Anathema use their profane magics to learn of these new Moon Mad and send forth their minions to capture them, so it is imperative to get there quickly.<br /> <br /> 2. Knowledge is key. All Silver Anathema have an identifying mark upon their bodies that cannot be altered, the Tell, so it is paramount to watch for this, but do not discount any other information that can be gleaned. The demon often retains the memories and some of the relationships held by their host body for a time after possession. These ties can be used to lure out the Anathema from their lair, to determine their likely habits and strategies, and what goals they might initially pursue. However, be forewarned. The warping that occurs when the demon takes a new host is most severe in the Silver Anathema, such that the final demon may not retain anything of the original host, not in body, mind, or soul. <br /> <br /> 3. Nearly every Wyld Hunt that has pursued a Silver Anathema has lost it at one point or another. Do not think of this as failure, but as another opportunity to learn. Most young Moon Mad instinctively know to steal the form of a bird or fish as soon as they can, but most only gain one form. When they change, watch their new form as much as you can, both to learn its markings and to see their Tell. This will help you to take them down a second time.<br /> <br /> 4. Practice hunting. Learn to track, hunt, and kill every animal under the sun, so that you cannot be surprised later. Learn the habits of animals, such that you may spot them acting strangely or flush them out depriving the Anathema of their concealment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this, it feels like something I can see NPCs saying in a game. I Bess copy it for me notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:40:08-08:00","id":1294622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294620#post1294620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The advantage from being tiny is whoever is trying to spot you loses 2 successes. Everything else you are describing is circumstantial, and benefits non lunars just as much as lunars.<br /> <br /> If the lunar is not invested in dexterity and stealth then they are definitely at risk of being spotted by a dragonblooded who is invested in awareness. Especially if you consider the escalating penalties of -3/-4/-5 if you are attempting to go to ground, or just the -3 penalty for attempting stealth in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hiding amidsts a wave of a thousand bats in the middle of the night while also in the form of a bat benefits the Wyld Hunt as much as the Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:56:08-08:00","id":1294623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294622#post1294622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hiding amidsts a wave of a thousand bats in the middle of the night while also in the form of a bat benefits the Wyld Hunt as much as the Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? Stop moving goal posts. This is hardly a general circumstance and ond heavily weighted in favour of the lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T23:56:53-08:00","id":1294624,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto... This is getting more and more contrived.<br /> <br /> Most lunars aren't fully rational optimising bots. Their charms are going to be scattered and non focused. Their panicking and under stress by the wyld hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T00:39:36-08:00","id":1294628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294623#post1294623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously? Stop moving goal posts. This is hardly a general circumstance and ond heavily weighted in favour of the lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not moving goal posts, Lunars often Lair in caves and serious wilderness. If you have ever lived even remotely in the country you would know it\u2019s trivially easy to scare any nearby cluster of birds, it\u2019s a simple stunt and one the Lunar would cultivate rather easy if so inclined and even if they weren\u2019t it\u2019s a consequence of living in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> What do you honestly consider a general circumstance? Do your view in Lunars have them all live in a village or small town? The vast majority of Lunars that I have read that have mentioned their homes involves them lairing in distant manses or deep wild areas, Gerd Marrow Eater, Lilith, Magnificent Jaguar.<br /> <br /> What do you consider a general Lunar home? Is it an apartment in Nexus? Maybe if the Lunar is wearing someone\u2019s skin...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s weighed in Favor if Lunars because Lunars don\u2019t Sleep under Bridges with giant moonsilver signs saying don\u2019t ambush me I\u2019m sleeping, and if they did it\u2019s probably a trap.<br /> <br /> <br /> No seriously what do you consider a suitable general Lunar home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T00:43:58-08:00","id":1294629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294624#post1294624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eldagusto... This is getting more and more contrived.<br /> <br /> Most lunars aren't fully rational optimising bots. Their charms are going to be scattered and non focused. Their panicking and under stress by the wyld hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve not mentioned any optimization, and I\u2019ve barely mentioned charms this whole discussion. Most of the discussion involved a few basic hearts blood forms, some simple survival precautions and general trickery they are known for. What are you talking about with he Optimizebot talk.<br /> <br /> At best I implied the use of excellences and things like Emerald Grasshopper form.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve not even delved deep into this being a beefed out Lunar. I\u2019ve pointed out general Lunar capabilities, and the fact most Lunars are mysterious entities because it\u2019s hard to keep track of someone who specifically shape shifts when traveling and sleeping to keep a low profile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T00:49:25-08:00","id":1294631,"title":"","content":"Well, jumping to the home point, a Lunar who lives in an underground area can have their exits sealed on them. You take your time, try to collapse as many entrances as you can before going down to fight the Lunar. If they're in an aboveground ruin,and have a bird shape, cornering them is much harder but still doable if you can bring sheer weight of numbers into it. One guy might not be able to hit a swarm of flying bats escaping, even one Dragon Blood would have problems with that... but a battle group of well trained archers, with Dragon Blooded supervision? Even if they don't hit the Lunar, they're going to down pretty much all the rest of the swarm with one volley, leaving the Wood Aspect bowman with only one mark to focus on instead of dozens. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T00:51:02-08:00","id":1294632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294628#post1294628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not moving goal posts, Lunars often Lair in caves and serious wilderness. If you have ever lived even remotely in the country you would know it\u2019s trivially easy to scare any nearby cluster of birds, it\u2019s a simple stunt and one the Lunar would cultivate rather easy if so inclined and even if they weren\u2019t it\u2019s a consequence of living in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> What do you honestly consider a general circumstance? Do your view in Lunars have them all live in a village or small town? The vast majority of Lunars that I have read that have mentioned their homes involves them lairing in distant manses or deep wild areas, Gerd Marrow Eater, Lilith, Magnificent Jaguar.<br /> <br /> What do you consider a general Lunar home? Is it an apartment in Nexus? Maybe if the Lunar is wearing someone\u2019s skin...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s weighed in Favor if Lunars because Lunars don\u2019t Sleep under Bridges with giant moonsilver signs saying don\u2019t ambush me I\u2019m sleeping, and if they did it\u2019s probably a trap.<br /> <br /> <br /> No seriously what do you consider a suitable general Lunar home?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the question is &quot;How does a wyld hunt ever corner lunars in their lairs?&quot; In which case go ahead sure they get a home ground advantage. You don't win a war sitting at home though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:04:14-08:00","id":1294633,"title":"","content":"Elda, you are absolutely moving things around. You are getting reasonable answers, and then you're going &quot;but what if the Lunar can counter that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, then they friggin' counter it. Sheesh.<br /> <br /> If we are to take the dominion writeups as an example, Wyld Hunt do reach even elder Lunars, who tend to survive them for the reasons you mention.<br /> <br /> Most Lunars are not elder Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:10:27-08:00","id":1294634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294631#post1294631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, jumping to the home point, a Lunar who lives in an underground area can have their exits sealed on them. You take your time, try to collapse as many entrances as you can before going down to fight the Lunar. If they're in an aboveground ruin,and have a bird shape, cornering them is much harder but still doable if you can bring sheer weight of numbers into it. One guy might not be able to hit a swarm of flying bats escaping, even one Dragon Blood would have problems with that... but a battle group of well trained archers, with Dragon Blooded supervision? Even if they don't hit the Lunar, they're going to down pretty much all the rest of the swarm with one volley, leaving the Wood Aspect bowman with only one mark to focus on instead of dozens. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See this is a better plan. But question, in 3rd ed do Lunars automatically return to human form when dying? And what do you do when you say only have one or two Dragonblooded with super senses, and they are killed or incapacitated early on? You block off the cave and smoke/flood it, but what if you don\u2019t find the Lunars corpse? Even in the real world theirs stories where say the military chase natives into the hills or mountains and block the exits but still don\u2019t find their quarry. And these are normal humans who can\u2019t shapeshift.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s one of the more reasonable strategies, but there is a lot of room for it to go wrong.<br /> <br /> Like on average how many casualties do you expect from a Wyld Hunt? I\u2019m being Generous and assuming a Wyld Hunt of at least 10 Exalted, but the books mention dire situations with only a Fellowship of 5 Dragonblooded on some Hunts.<br /> <br /> What do you do if the Lunar has Demons, it\u2019s not unreasonable considering one third of the Castes are No Moons. Or how do you even ambush a Lunar who has a good working relationship with the Spirit court of their area, whether it\u2019s a forest or mountain or desert.<br /> <br /> And if you take a Shikari into the deep Wilderness away from supply lines you can\u2019t silently bring an Army all into a close combat and get the drop on a Lunar, unless you set a trap or you have an inside man. If the Lunar lures you on a wild goose chase mortals will only slow you down and they will rub out of supplies. But without mortal shocktroops it\u2019s much more dangerous for Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Like if a Lunar lives on a Plateau in a desert or Canyon don\u2019t expect to ambush them with an army when they will notice you miles before you see them. If a Lunar maims your Horses and Camels (which a a Lunar or any Exalt really can do with a number of methods from arrows, to traps, stealth hamstringing, only a handful of the Wyld Hunt will be able to keep up with the Lunar, unless the Lunar flies away then really you probably won\u2019t be able to catch up with one that starts at long or Extreme range bands away.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s sounding more and more you aren\u2019t going to Surprise a Lunar unless you are very lucky, or they make a foolish mistake like they put faith in mortals or gods who betray them or they sleep Naked in the middle of the Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:15:59-08:00","id":1294635,"title":"","content":"Well, El, you keep jumping to these very specific scenarios in a way that views them as instant win scenarios and then when someone says they aren't you tend to say they are because of a massive amount of these things and it invariable would require the extermination of all life in a ten mile radius to even hope to get the Lunar. Like the idea of a Lunar having a burrowing form was met with being pointed out that tunneling isn't the fastest method of transportation, so you could be tracked and attacked with some difficulty. To which you argued there would invariably be a massive network of pre-existing tunnels so the Lunar is only digging a few inches before they hit their escape network and would be so stable and intricate that it would even foil an earthquake being generated by an earth aspect in the area. <br /> <br /> Then the one you've come back to a few times is this idea of a Lunar hanging out with countless of some flying animal that at the drop of a hat the Lunar will be able to have scatter in a near blinding cloud while the Lunar turns into one of those animals and escapes in the cloud. Ignoring that the Lunar would actually have a very narrow point in time where they could use this trick since these animals would likely scatter at the first sign of danger meaning that unless you were already one of these things they'd have to hope they can shift before the animals all get away plus get their movement to leave and hope that this happens before the Hunt gets their attacks off potentially damaging the Lunar in a way that makes the escape harder or does something to lock down the flight method. Basically you keep discussing a scenario that seems to hinge on the idea that the Lunar has been fortifying and designing their home to have an extremely elaborate bug out system solely for the purpose that when the hunt shows up they can mentally laugh from among the pigeons and fly off as opposed to just leaving before the Hunt arrives. <br /> <br /> Like most Lunars are not going to plan this. Hell most Wyld Hunts are probably going to be dealing with a Lunar on their own hunt either because the Lunar wants a new form, in the process of learning their own powers, or because a new Lunar is likely to be dealing with their rage in which case someone(s) or something(s) are in the process of getting the Lunar's near undivided unattention in dealing with it. (Ie the Wyld Hunt probably was alerted when the local bandit population started getting ripped apart by an angry mooseman.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:18:48-08:00","id":1294636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294633#post1294633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elda, you are absolutely moving things around. You are getting reasonable answers, and then you're going &amp;quot;but what if the Lunar can counter that?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Well, then they friggin' counter it. Sheesh.<br /> <br /> If we are to take the dominion writeups as an example, Wyld Hunt do reach even elder Lunars, who tend to survive them for the reasons you mention.<br /> <br /> Most Lunars are not elder Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broham I\u2019m not. I\u2019m pointing out sometimes these are sound, like the trapping a Lunar Underground strategy, but I\u2019m also pointing out a lot can go wrong and it\u2019s far to expensive and silly most of the time for the realm to to send Wyld Hunts on Lunars unless their Sidereal Handlers have specific situational knowledge to lead them to believe their plan would succeed, or the Lunar is initiating last stand protocols, which is a reason a lot of Lunar Elders are stated to have died.<br /> <br /> My basic points still stand, you need to ambush a Lunar if you don\u2019t want them to flee, otherwise unless they want to stay it\u2019s relatively easy for them to evade a Wyld Hunt. And even if you Ambush one, there is still a reasonable chance it won\u2019t work.<br /> <br /> And if their is more then one Lunar, or other Exalt, and especially if you aren\u2019t expecting them most Wyld Hunt can rather easily fail against two or three Exalts rather then one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:26:51-08:00","id":1294637,"title":"","content":"Um... Most lunars are new at this. And I think you're giving the terrestrial too little credit. They trained. They worked. And they have experience in this.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial may be weaker than lunars in a fair fight... But this ain't fair. They got age gaps. Numbers. Sidereal assistance. Mortal auxiliaries. Artifacts and sorceries. Spirit allies. Sorcerous workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:34:53-08:00","id":1294638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294635#post1294635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, El, you keep jumping to these very specific scenarios in a way that views them as instant win scenarios and then when someone says they aren't you tend to say they are because of a massive amount of these things and it invariable would require the extermination of all life in a ten mile radius to even hope to get the Lunar. Like the idea of a Lunar having a burrowing form was met with being pointed out that tunneling isn't the fastest method of transportation, so you could be tracked and attacked with some difficulty. To which you argued there would invariably be a massive network of pre-existing tunnels so the Lunar is only digging a few inches before they hit their escape network and would be so stable and intricate that it would even foil an earthquake being generated by an earth aspect in the area. <br /> <br /> Then the one you've come back to a few times is this idea of a Lunar hanging out with countless of some flying animal that at the drop of a hat the Lunar will be able to have scatter in a near blinding cloud while the Lunar turns into one of those animals and escapes in the cloud. Ignoring that the Lunar would actually have a very narrow point in time where they could use this trick since these animals would likely scatter at the first sign of danger meaning that unless you were already one of these things they'd have to hope they can shift before the animals all get away plus get their movement to leave and hope that this happens before the Hunt gets their attacks off potentially damaging the Lunar in a way that makes the escape harder or does something to lock down the flight method. Basically you keep discussing a scenario that seems to hinge on the idea that the Lunar has been fortifying and designing their home to have an extremely elaborate bug out system solely for the purpose that when the hunt shows up they can mentally laugh from among the pigeons and fly off as opposed to just leaving before the Hunt arrives. <br /> <br /> Like most Lunars are not going to plan this. Hell most Wyld Hunts are probably going to be dealing with a Lunar on their own hunt either because the Lunar wants a new form, in the process of learning their own powers, or because a new Lunar is likely to be dealing with their rage in which case someone(s) or something(s) are in the process of getting the Lunar's near undivided unattention in dealing with it. (Ie the Wyld Hunt probably was alerted when the local bandit population started getting ripped apart by an angry mooseman.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m just saying a lot of things can go wrong when you hunt down Lunars. I\u2019m accepting some strategies are really good, which is part of why I started this thread I wanted discussion of various strategies both parties would use.<br /> <br /> Why would you get pissed off by me listing multiple examples of clusters of animals, it\u2019s literally a huge ass trope of cinema and novels to be distracted by animals in the wild when hunting, and if you can shapeshift why wouldn\u2019t you use that. I bring it up because it\u2019s a valid tactic, even cities have waves pigeons.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s literally a thing for Lunars not wanting to die because they get mobbed by a terrestrial or celestial hit squad. And you either have an army and therefore can\u2019t sneak fast and have to Block off a Lunar or you send a smaller team but have less firepower.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why would you get upset I\u2019m asking for strategies, and then I posit viable counter strategies. Is it really unreasonable for shapeshifters to shapeshift? And a 3-6 second time window is all a Lunar will need to complicate most plan.<br /> <br /> I mean I\u2019ve found this thread helpful. I\u2019m sorry if discussion pisses some people off. I think it\u2019s useful in assessing the system.<br /> <br /> But if I\u2019m playing devils advocate why would people be upset that I\u2019m... advocating for the devil... that the whole point of this thought exercise and discussion.<br /> <br /> I mean I\u2019m not discussing the other way around, because there\u2019s too many people for Lunars to seek Vengence from, and if they are Dragonblooded a patient Lunar would likely succeed unless they are the head of a House, and even then they have a reasonable chance of succeeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:44:09-08:00","id":1294639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294637#post1294637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... Most lunars are new at this. And I think you're giving the terrestrial too little credit. They trained. They worked. And they have experience in this.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial may be weaker than lunars in a fair fight... But this ain't fair. They got age gaps. Numbers. Sidereal assistance. Mortal auxiliaries. Artifacts and sorceries. Spirit allies. Sorcerous workings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I\u2019m literally stacking the deck in Favor of the Wyld Hunt in the general assumption of this thread. With the idea of a prepare Wyld Hunt has at least ten Exalted ( with maybe one of them secretly being Sidereal).<br /> <br /> And the age gap isn\u2019t certain, I left that ambiguous in this situation because I wanted to discuss multiple situations. If the Lunar hasn\u2019t met other Lunars and they are a year into their 2nd Breath yeah they are screwed, for one because they probably know very little about other Exalted Period, especially not the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> But those situations I\u2019m acknowledging yeah a baby Lunar is really their safest bet.<br /> <br /> But where does it say most Lunars are brand new? It\u2019s insane to think over 200 Lunars die a year!? No a lot of Lunars are new, but i highly doubt most are.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s reasonable to assume a Lunar could be as old as the Dragons hunting em. A century old Lunar ain\u2019t nothing special, a thousand year old Lunar yeah, but living to be a Hundred is not noteable at all.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not even arguing Lunars stomp a Wyld Hunt, I\u2019m simply saying they need to check off a lot of Boxes before they have a reasonable even 50/50 chance plan for a Lunar Campaign. And what\u2019s the point of holding an expensive Wyld Hunt if they fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:47:06-08:00","id":1294641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294638#post1294638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m just saying a lot of things can go wrong when you hunt down Lunars. I\u2019m accepting some strategies are really good, which is part of why I started this thread I wanted discussion of various strategies both parties would use.<br /> <br /> Why would you get pissed off by me listing multiple examples of clusters of animals, it\u2019s literally a huge ass trope of cinema and novels to be distracted by animals in the wild when hunting, and if you can shapeshift why wouldn\u2019t you use that. I bring it up because it\u2019s a valid tactic, even cities have waves pigeons.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s literally a thing for Lunars not wanting to die because they get mobbed by a terrestrial or celestial hit squad. And you either have an army and therefore can\u2019t sneak fast and have to Block off a Lunar or you send a smaller team but have less firepower.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why would you get upset I\u2019m asking for strategies, and then I posit viable counter strategies. Is it really unreasonable for shapeshifters to shapeshift? And a 3-6 second time window is all a Lunar will need to complicate most plan.<br /> <br /> I mean I\u2019ve found this thread helpful. I\u2019m sorry if discussion pisses some people off. I think it\u2019s useful in assessing the system.<br /> <br /> But if I\u2019m playing devils advocate why would people be upset that I\u2019m... advocating for the devil... that the whole point of this thought exercise and discussion.<br /> <br /> I mean I\u2019m not discussing the other way around, because there\u2019s too many people for Lunars to seek Vengence from, and if they are Dragonblooded a patient Lunar would likely succeed unless they are the head of a House, and even then they have a reasonable chance of succeeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>One not getting upset, However, you are being frustrating because you seem to be either fishing for a 100% flawless tactic against any Lunar as opposed to just the initial premise which was how does the Hunt stop a Lunar from running, except you're basically whiterooming this. Like the last one you said, &quot;Oh its a good plan, but it fails if the Lunar is a sorcerer.&quot; Or that the Wyld Hunt fails in an attack on a Lunar if it turns there's more than one Lunar, or the Lunar has a bunch of other exalt allies. Yes you are moving goal posts because this is not being presented, &quot;Hey I'm being reasonable and just pointing out that it's hard to stop a determined Lunar from running if they want to&quot; its being presented as, &quot;The Wyld Hunt is stupid and doesn't work because they can't actually corner or stop a Lunar because of course any reasonable Lunar would do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ignoring the fact that Lunars are driven by their own Rage and agenda which would be problematic if you kept having to flee at the drop of a hat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-07-2019, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:57:16-08:00","id":1294642,"title":"","content":"The Hunt could also very well be the ones laying the trap. &quot;Oh noooo look at this supply chain! It's wide open! Now how did this happen that such a vital part of our military operation is so woefully unguarded? It'd be a real shame if some Lunar came along and- SURPRISE a dozen dragonblooded hidden in the wagons and among the soldiers!&quot;<br /> <br /> And, of course, you wait until they've already spent a decent chunk of essence trashing the place before striking. Double points if you reveal only 1-2 DBs off the start, making it look like a totally inept ambush, so the Lunar doesn't just run, he stays and fights, thinking &quot;well this is great, now I get to whittle down the Dynasty too&quot;. THEN the other ten terrestrials bust out and the Lunar realizes that it's time to leave. Of course imperial highways being what they are, the trees are cut back 100 yards for safety, so your best bet is becoming something that can hide in the grass, like a vole. So you become a vole, but unfortunately there's a DB there who can spot the fleas on a dogs back from 50 paces, and who also has Eye of Blazing Truth, so twin lances of fire streak out from her eyes, strike your little vole body and set it brilliantly ablaze for enough time for everyone else to pile on arrows, chakrams and smash their great hammers around. At which point you're probably dead.<br /> <br /> But maybe not! Maybe you just barely got out of the way of most of those attacks and voles can burrow, so you scramble into the ground. You're really badly hurt, but that's okay, you're alive. But only for a few moments, because another half dozen creatures burrow in from above to lance you with diamond needles. Vaktri elemental assassins, they can sense anything moving through the ground via their Earthsense ability, and have supernatural tunneling and piercing attacks.<br /> <br /> That sounds like an unreasonable amount of firepower and contingencies, and maybe for post-empress disappearance it is, but that's a totally plausible thing for the Realm to do. A dozen DBs isn't even 0.001% of the DBs in the Realm, and summoning a half dozen elementals is less than a week's work for a skilled sorcerer. The size and power of the Realm is crushing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:04:36-08:00","id":1294643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294639#post1294639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019m literally stacking the deck in Favor of the Wyld Hunt in the general assumption of this thread. With the idea of a prepare Wyld Hunt has at least ten Exalted ( with maybe one of them secretly being Sidereal).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are assuming an encounter occurs in the lunars territory in the middle of the night with nearby bats with the lunar having a bat as one of their forms and you are claiming to be stacking the deck in favor of the hunt?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:14:52-08:00","id":1294644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294641#post1294641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One not getting upset, However, you are being frustrating because you seem to be either fishing for a 100% flawless tactic against any Lunar as opposed to just the initial premise which was how does the Hunt stop a Lunar from running, except you're basically whiterooming this. Like the last one you said, &amp;quot;Oh its a good plan, but it fails if the Lunar is a sorcerer.&amp;quot; Or that the Wyld Hunt fails in an attack on a Lunar if it turns there's more than one Lunar, or the Lunar has a bunch of other exalt allies. Yes you are moving goal posts because this is not being presented, &amp;quot;Hey I'm being reasonable and just pointing out that it's hard to stop a determined Lunar from running if they want to&amp;quot; its being presented as, &amp;quot;The Wyld Hunt is stupid and doesn't work because they can't actually corner or stop a Lunar because of course any reasonable Lunar would do this.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Ignoring the fact that Lunars are driven by their own Rage and agenda which would be problematic if you kept having to flee at the drop of a hat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this is literally the opposite of a white room scenario.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not expecting Lunars to be Sorcerers it was kind of a side question, because that is literally the point of this thread to poke around and examine scenarios. Wyld Hunts are mentioned to usually have at least one Sorcerer but at the same time the only examples of Demons and Elementals being employed in the Hunt are given with famous Sorcerers like friggin Mnemon. Demons are mentioned a lot in the books but in specific situations they are very under used, so I just posited what the hell donrhey do when a Lunar has Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not even pointing out all these methods will always succeed. I am stating though that it\u2019s my intention to figure out how many contingencies do Wyld Hunts in general, as well as specific hardcore ones, have.<br /> <br /> The Summoner and Extra Exalts were literally side questions, this whole thread is a discussion and I brought up the idea early on and no one discussed it, I bring it up again and now for some reason it\u2019s fristr or insulting? That is the whole point of this thread. I want to know the contingencies planned Hunts have and extemporaneously gathered Hunts have.<br /> <br /> And what do they do if they are unlucky. Yes you could spot a Lunar hiding behind animal distractions that is flying away, but it\u2019s also feasible you miss, or the Lunar tanks it and after getting a certain distance away only has to worry about one or two specific Shikari and escaping two Dragonblooded is much more feasible then escaping ten.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still nobody has really brought up methods for how you sneak up a whole Wyld Hunt into even Short range of a Lunar I\u2019d they Lair in a defensible hill or mountain or spire. Flat out what are their methods of approach? Do they get a single scout to wait till the Lunar Leaves and then roll up and set a trap? If so they have to know they won\u2019t be caught. Do they charge the tower/mountain? If so the Lunar can cheese it well before you get there. These are the points of discussion I am curious about.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not calling th Wyld Hunt stupid, geesh, I am saying it would be beneficial to discuss what they do in certain scenarios. Say the Hunt Enters the Woods or caves or whateve. They are probably not getting to close range with the Lunar before they are spotted. At the same time are they analyzing every butterfly and squirrel? Because if they aren\u2019t it could be the Lunar, if they are what if they are just distracting themselves while the Lunar does something else. Seriously it\u2019s a good question. Most of these were assuming non specialized Lunars. If the Lunar was specialized in stealth, Hell they wouldn\u2019t necessarily be in animal form. How many snipers do you have? How many dashers Who can close in? How many super senses having Matt Murdock\u2019s? Everyone isn\u2019t good at everything. So every time a Dragonblooded is compromised their strategies get limited.<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunts Against Solars May work because Solars are essentially all brand new babies, and generally they are more straight forward and probably won\u2019t shapeshift. But a Lunar has a lot more unknowns. So unless it\u2019s a specific Lunar like they got lucky and the country next door reports a mooseman eating their king and a rag tag 7-12 Dragons are assembled for a Wyld Hunt they could probably Scalp the cub. But. Otherwise they only seem to work when they know the Lunar will not abandon its territory or project or people, and they are probably experienced Lunars and you know you can more or less have a straight up battle to the death, not necessarily a dual but an actual battle of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:19:50-08:00","id":1294645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294642#post1294642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunt could also very well be the ones laying the trap. &amp;quot;Oh noooo look at this supply chain! It's wide open! Now how did this happen that such a vital part of our military operation is so woefully unguarded? It'd be a real shame if some Lunar came along and- SURPRISE a dozen dragonblooded hidden in the wagons and among the soldiers!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And, of course, you wait until they've already spent a decent chunk of essence trashing the place before striking. Double points if you reveal only 1-2 DBs off the start, making it look like a totally inept ambush, so the Lunar doesn't just run, he stays and fights, thinking &amp;quot;well this is great, now I get to whittle down the Dynasty too&amp;quot;. THEN the other ten terrestrials bust out and the Lunar realizes that it's time to leave. Of course imperial highways being what they are, the trees are cut back 100 yards for safety, so your best bet is becoming something that can hide in the grass, like a vole. So you become a vole, but unfortunately there's a DB there who can spot the fleas on a dogs back from 50 paces, and who also has Eye of Blazing Truth, so twin lances of fire streak out from her eyes, strike your little vole body and set it brilliantly ablaze for enough time for everyone else to pile on arrows, chakrams and smash their great hammers around. At which point you're probably dead.<br /> <br /> But maybe not! Maybe you just barely got out of the way of most of those attacks and voles can burrow, so you scramble into the ground. You're really badly hurt, but that's okay, you're alive. But only for a few moments, because another half dozen creatures burrow in from above to lance you with diamond needles. Vaktri elemental assassins, they can sense anything moving through the ground via their Earthsense ability, and have supernatural tunneling and piercing attacks.<br /> <br /> That sounds like an unreasonable amount of firepower and contingencies, and maybe for post-empress disappearance it is, but that's a totally plausible thing for the Realm to do. A dozen DBs isn't even 0.001% of the DBs in the Realm, and summoning a half dozen elementals is less than a week's work for a skilled sorcerer. The size and power of the Realm is crushing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that\u2019s not unreasonable that is literally the level of tactic and preparedness I\u2019m expecting for when things go correct, and when they do tag some Silver Pact Elders. So I\u2019m asking how often do you think they set up plans this well? Are they Stu\u2019s prepared because they really think they can trick the Lunar or do they really go all in on the Trap \u201cbecause\u201d they want to tag a specific Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:26:24-08:00","id":1294646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294643#post1294643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are assuming an encounter occurs in the lunars territory in the middle of the night with nearby bats with the lunar having a bat as one of their forms and you are claiming to be stacking the deck in favor of the hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that\u2019s a very general and reasonable scenario. Say they know the Lunar sometimes sleeps there, sleeping at night is reasonable, bats live in caves, forests and mountains, if a Lunar is Lairing somewhere it\u2019s reasonable to assume they investing in a few of the local wildlife, not everyone just spends their heart blood libraries on Platypus/Starfish/Capybara/Seahorse/Zebra.<br /> <br /> What part of that scenario is unreasonable? Remove night time if you want, caves are still dark, remove bats you still have mice or geckos or moths or boars or squirrels.<br /> <br /> Honestly you don\u2019t think it\u2019s stacking the deck in the Wyld Hunts favor when I\u2019m assuming they have like 9 Dragonblooded one Secret Sidereal, and dozens if not hundreds of mortal Soldiers.<br /> <br /> Come on be real. Contribute to the discussion, no need to harp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:30:39-08:00","id":1294647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294645#post1294645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No that\u2019s not unreasonable that is literally the level of tactic and preparedness I\u2019m expecting for when things go correct, and when they do tag some Silver Pact Elders. So I\u2019m asking how often do you think they set up plans this well? Are they Stu\u2019s prepared because they really think they can trick the Lunar or do they really go all in on the Trap \u201cbecause\u201d they want to tag a specific Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very often. <br /> <br /> Those counterarguments and tactics you bring out? Will work very well. Against mortals.<br /> <br /> But these ain't normal. These are Terrestrial Exalted, Princes of the Earth. They outnumber the lunar at least 20 times over. With several dozen more advantages.<br /> <br /> And they aren't going in blind. They know. They have sidereal Intel and institutional knowledge of millenia. They know the easy tricks. The things a lunar would go to first. And that's how they kill him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:39:32-08:00","id":1294648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294645#post1294645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No that\u2019s not unreasonable that is literally the level of tactic and preparedness I\u2019m expecting for when things go correct, and when they do tag some Silver Pact Elders. So I\u2019m asking how often do you think they set up plans this well? Are they Stu\u2019s prepared because they really think they can trick the Lunar or do they really go all in on the Trap \u201cbecause\u201d they want to tag a specific Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they might just go as all in as they can as often as they can. Wyld Hunts aren\u2019t the only thing DBs ever do, but especially houses Ledaal, Mnemon, Cathak, Tepet and Peleps go pretty hard. The first part of the Wyld Hunt might even be like the Inquisition from warhammer 40k, catspaws and subterfuge, spy networks, feeling out who this Lunar is, what will she die defending, what are her preferred strategies and known forms, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Not every Wyld Hunt is like that, obviously, some are just formed totally out of the blue in the field because time is so sensitive. Gotta get the young Lunar before the old Lunars do. If you\u2019re hunting a mature and established Lunar though, time is not really of the essence, they\u2019re not going to become vastly more powerful in 4-5 weeks. You can take your time, rally a dozen or more terrestrials, sorcerers, snipers, spymasters, infiltrators, poisoners, all the god awful bastards that the Dynasty has at their fingertips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:42:07-08:00","id":1294649,"title":"","content":"But thing is Lunars generally aren\u2019t that predictable, it\u2019s more of finding a sweet spot of a Lunar being predictable and having access to the controlled conditions reliably jump them, and that is more likely the closer you are to the realm, or Prasad because they are badasses.<br /> <br /> But again what about when Lunars travel in groups? They become exponentially more Dangerous and resourceful. So you either have to have found something precious to the whole pack, or really got lucky.<br /> <br /> I mean it\u2019s not completely a one way street, Lunars have assassinated Dynasts on the Blessed Isle and even rarer assassinated Sidereals in Heaven.<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunt Tactics can still work on a couple Lunars but what about a pack of Five? Five experienced Celestials can have any number of resources. The War with the Bull is an Example of attacking a Circle of moderately experienced Exalts and it became a nations spanning endeavor that ruined House Tepet. Normal Wyld Hunts don\u2019t have the resources I handle a pack of 5 Lunars, and they would need serious Throne Backing. Which makes me wonder now that they know the Empress is gone Lunars could Cluster in a reasonable sized pack 4-6 and really they would need a major military Campaign to handle them.<br /> <br /> Edit: it was addressed to Accelerator.<br /> <br /> Badass post though Doc!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":". 03-07-2019, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:48:19-08:00","id":1294650,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is a Wyld Hunt that fails to catch and kill the Lunar isn't necessarily a failure. If an Anathema is a potential growing threat on your doorstep then chasing it off, killing it's beastman devotees, forcing it's spirit allies to submit to Immaculate might, pulling down and destroying any evidence of it's vile artifice, pacifying the population and demonstrating to nearby allies the dedication of the Realm to protecting the world from horrifying demon-cannibals is probably a pretty big win, even without a corpse that was glowing silver a few minutes ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:50:29-08:00","id":1294651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294646#post1294646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that\u2019s a very general and reasonable scenario. Say they know the Lunar sometimes sleeps there, sleeping at night is reasonable, bats live in caves, forests and mountains, if a Lunar is Lairing somewhere it\u2019s reasonable to assume they investing in a few of the local wildlife, not everyone just spends their heart blood libraries on Platypus/Starfish/Capybara/Seahorse/Zebra.<br /> <br /> What part of that scenario is unreasonable? Remove night time if you want, caves are still dark, remove bats you still have mice or geckos or moths or boars or squirrels.<br /> <br /> Honestly you don\u2019t think it\u2019s stacking the deck in the Wyld Hunts favor when I\u2019m assuming they have like 9 Dragonblooded one Secret Sidereal, and dozens if not hundreds of mortal Soldiers.<br /> <br /> Come on be real. Contribute to the discussion, no need to harp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What discussion? hypothetical what ifs that could go on forever? It would get tiring quickly and any blanks that I don't fill in you will jump on to fill with your counter strategies to portray circumstance in their advantage. You are taking a &quot;reasonable&quot; scenario then portraying it as an outcome for &quot;all&quot; scenarios. These assumptions you are saying you made you have not even mentioned until recently. <br /> <br /> I attempted to engage more but I am not stepping beyond the initial goal post that you set. Your presentation of the assumption that the encounter is occurring in the Lunars Territory was the goal post moving. This is the crux of the issue.<br /> <br /> How does the Wild Hunt ever corner Lunars? - Simple. The Wild Hunt does not need to engage in the Lunar territory. They end up encountering the lunar outside their territory. Perhaps the lunar was on a raid and underestimated the opponents strength. Then they could not escape. Maybe they do manage a coordinated enough attack with understanding the lunars strength with enough research. Perhaps in their essence fever they overestimated their own capability. Perhaps their bond to their solar mate drew them out to a compromising position. Perhaps they actually want to leave their territory to wage war on the realm.<br /> <br /> I am not stepping into a hypothetical scenario where for some reason the Hunt has to engage within the lunars territory. Especially if there is no understanding of what the lunar is capable of before they go there. Without defining the situation of what the lunar is capable of it just leaves any hypothesising down to &quot;but the lunar has xxx prepared&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T02:53:48-08:00","id":1294652,"title":"","content":"4-5 Lunars in one place is a much bigger effort, but also nets a much bigger reward. That number almost certainly represents the better part of a school, and if you can wipe out a whole school of Lunars you\u2019ve set the Pact back in that area by, I don\u2019t even know, centuries? That\u2019s where you don\u2019t send in the dozen DBs, that\u2019s where you send in immaculate masters and an entire circle of Bronze Faction Sidereal assassins. It\u2019s super risky, because if you lose that confrontation you\u2019ve lost some of your greatest assets, but the rewards are likewise great.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason the Battle of Futile Blood was so bad is that the 7 Solars that they confronted in that battle also had a teardrinker army, internal political problems and gold faction Sidereal sabotage. Even THEN it was really bad for the Bull too. Remember, the Tepet legions we\u2019re intentionally fed to the Bull as a way of knocking down Tepet\u2019s power in relation to the other houses, they were never meant to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:00:25-08:00","id":1294653,"title":"","content":"If the Lunar turns into a bird and flies away in a flock, she gets a great view of the tribe she was training being slaughtered, her demesne overrun, and gets to hear her wife and kids being taken away in chains.<br /> <br /> Congrats, Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:09:33-08:00","id":1294654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294652#post1294652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4-5 Lunars in one place is a much bigger effort, but also nets a much bigger reward. That number almost certainly represents the better part of a school, and if you can wipe out a whole school of Lunars you\u2019ve set the Pact back in that area by, I don\u2019t even know, centuries? That\u2019s where you don\u2019t send in the dozen DBs, that\u2019s where you send in immaculate masters and an entire circle of Bronze Faction Sidereal assassins. It\u2019s super risky, because if you lose that confrontation you\u2019ve lost some of your greatest assets, but the rewards are likewise great.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason the Battle of Futile Blood was so bad is that the 7 Solars that they confronted in that battle also had a teardrinker army, internal political problems and gold faction Sidereal sabotage. Even THEN it was really bad for the Bull too. Remember, the Tepet legions we\u2019re intentionally fed to the Bull as a way of knocking down Tepet\u2019s power in relation to the other houses, they were never meant to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>7? I thought it was five.<br /> <br /> Yurgen Kaneko, the 2nd-highest-essence Dawn in Creation<br /> Samea, the highest-essence Zenith in Creation, and the most powerful sorcerer amongst the Solars<br /> Fear-Eater, Eclipse Shaman<br /> Nalla Bloodaxe, Night Caste<br /> A Twilight whose name I forget.<br /> <br /> They didn't have a Tear Eater army though, they had an Icewalker army of Tiger Warriors (though I assume they call them Mammoth warriors or something, not many Tigers up north), and some demons.<br /> In 2nd ed, also Haltans, Ourcastes and Warstriders, but I don't believe that's still the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:12:15-08:00","id":1294656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294654#post1294654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't have a Tear Eater army though, they had an Icewalker army of Tiger Warriors (though I assume they call them Mammoth warriors or something, not many Tigers up north), and some demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Siberian (Haslantian maybe, my Exalted geography/real world analogues isn't great) tigers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:15:19-08:00","id":1294657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294634#post1294634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See this is a better plan. But question, in 3rd ed do Lunars automatically return to human form when dying? And what do you do when you say only have one or two Dragonblooded with super senses, and they are killed or incapacitated early on? You block off the cave and smoke/flood it, but what if you don\u2019t find the Lunars corpse? Even in the real world theirs stories where say the military chase natives into the hills or mountains and block the exits but still don\u2019t find their quarry. And these are normal humans who can\u2019t shapeshift.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s one of the more reasonable strategies, but there is a lot of room for it to go wrong.<br /> <br /> Like on average how many casualties do you expect from a Wyld Hunt? I\u2019m being Generous and assuming a Wyld Hunt of at least 10 Exalted, but the books mention dire situations with only a Fellowship of 5 Dragonblooded on some Hunts.<br /> <br /> What do you do if the Lunar has Demons, it\u2019s not unreasonable considering one third of the Castes are No Moons. Or how do you even ambush a Lunar who has a good working relationship with the Spirit court of their area, whether it\u2019s a forest or mountain or desert.<br /> <br /> And if you take a Shikari into the deep Wilderness away from supply lines you can\u2019t silently bring an Army all into a close combat and get the drop on a Lunar, unless you set a trap or you have an inside man. If the Lunar lures you on a wild goose chase mortals will only slow you down and they will rub out of supplies. But without mortal shocktroops it\u2019s much more dangerous for Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Like if a Lunar lives on a Plateau in a desert or Canyon don\u2019t expect to ambush them with an army when they will notice you miles before you see them. If a Lunar maims your Horses and Camels (which a a Lunar or any Exalt really can do with a number of methods from arrows, to traps, stealth hamstringing, only a handful of the Wyld Hunt will be able to keep up with the Lunar, unless the Lunar flies away then really you probably won\u2019t be able to catch up with one that starts at long or Extreme range bands away.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s sounding more and more you aren\u2019t going to Surprise a Lunar unless you are very lucky, or they make a foolish mistake like they put faith in mortals or gods who betray them or they sleep Naked in the middle of the Road.</div> </div> </div> </div>A foolish mistake.. trusting people?<br /> <br /> El, it really sounds like you're arguing from the conclusion rather than the inverse. You're starting with the thesis than Lunars are hard to capture, and then concocting plans to justify it. They are difficult. But you're reaching here<br /> <br /> If you don't have anyone who can sense a Lunars tell, you are thorough when purging, and kill every animal they <i>might </i>be. While miniscule sized shapes are problematic, environmental attacks like flooding the place or fire and smoke should make it hard to keep them up. Maybe you miss them. If you do, the Hunt probably returns to civilization and remains for a bit in case the Lunar pops up again nearby<br /> <br /> Demons and spirits are not akin to omniscience. Plus they're enemies Shikari are going to be really good against due to the Immaculate Styles. <br /> <br /> If the Realm are in a position to 'corner' a Lunar, they've got supply lines and local resources. And you're right. It's going to be really hard to ambush a Lunar in their lair. So you either encircle the lair, or set a trap elsewhere. If you're fighting the Lunar head to head with battle groups and a Wyld Hunt, it's much harder to get away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:26:49-08:00","id":1294658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294651#post1294651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What discussion? hypothetical what ifs that could go on forever? It would get tiring quickly and any blanks that I don't fill in you will jump on to fill with your counter strategies to portray circumstance in their advantage. You are taking a &amp;quot;reasonable&amp;quot; scenario then portraying it as an outcome for &amp;quot;all&amp;quot; scenarios. These assumptions you are saying you made you have not even mentioned until recently. <br /> <br /> I attempted to engage more but I am not stepping beyond the initial goal post that you set. Your presentation of the assumption that the encounter is occurring in the Lunars Territory was the goal post moving. This is the crux of the issue.<br /> <br /> How does the Wild Hunt ever corner Lunars? - Simple. The Wild Hunt does not need to engage in the Lunar territory. They end up encountering the lunar outside their territory. Perhaps the lunar was on a raid and underestimated the opponents strength. Then they could not escape. Maybe they do manage a coordinated enough attack with understanding the lunars strength with enough research. Perhaps in their essence fever they overestimated their own capability. Perhaps their bond to their solar mate drew them out to a compromising position. Perhaps they actually want to leave their territory to wage war on the realm.<br /> <br /> I am not stepping into a hypothetical scenario where for some reason the Hunt has to engage within the lunars territory. Especially if there is no understanding of what the lunar is capable of before they go there. Without defining the situation of what the lunar is capable of it just leaves any hypothesising down to &amp;quot;but the lunar has xxx prepared&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mate the only thing close to a goalpost/thesis I believe I made was that Wyld Hunts need to either have a solid Ambush or get the Lunars to initiate a Last Stand Protocol. Everything else all the discussions they are open to change. The whole point of this thread is discussion, it isn\u2019t even a debate.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll note this thread would have been worthwhile just from the posts of Dr. Lovemonkey and Brilliantrain, they had excellent insight and they posted in a manner that inspired several ideas I want to try in a game.<br /> And even Slarn who provided counterpoints to my ideas seems to be enjoying the thread, sorry if I came off as uncool, I reread some of my replies and they may seem that way I appreciate your involvement in the discussion. And even the singular things have been useful like Heavyarms pointing out that Earth aspect tidbit or alucard talking about spells like DoOBs.<br /> <br /> Your coming at this like your trying to \u201cwin\u201d something and I\u2019m stating that is not the point of the thread. I will continue to point out hypotheticals if I find them useful.<br /> <br /> And I will point out if the Wyld Hunt Doesn\u2019t engage a Lunar in their Territory then there are some Lunars they can expect to never encounter. Some Lunars are Predicatable but flat out some folks you won\u2019t have the talent luck and resources to Ambush. And as mentioned Wyld Hunts have marched towards Mahasuchi\u2019s Nameless and earned a big L for it, so big they were slaughtered time and again. So yeah they do specifically do engage, especially with new Lunars. And it\u2019s pretty much standard operations for Solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Fact something to bring up the Wyld Hunt racks up their Ws by reliably exing out a cycle of 4-7ish Solar Exaltations that we\u2019re never Jade Prisoned, and only a handful of times did they get out of hand, like with Joachim, and then even more so with the Bull\u2019s Gang. Hunting Lunars, Raksha and Demons are the other Half. Raksha and Demons are hunted often because they are already trained in slaying the Unholy and they take it as duty, but the Military and questing Heroes also do this. Lunars are a big show of the Dynasty Flexing their Power. They Stomp out Lunars when Lunars try to challenge their territory, through raids or conquest, but also if they get lucky and fun new Lunars like they Hunt Solars, but they also hunt specific Lunars out of a spiritual imperative. Like who was that Bear Goddess Lunar they tracked down and slew to essentially show Immaculate dominance in the Northeast? These are the trickiest ones though. Some they slay because like that Bear Lunar they didn\u2019t want to abandon their people, but some are much trickier then that. Like you aren\u2019t going to take out Mahasuchi or Raksi without either a Multihouse Venture or the Enpresses full Backing, and even then you can get very mixed results or straight up loss like with the Bull.<br /> <br /> The lure them to you strategy is a very specific one that only will work on specific prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:30:16-08:00","id":1294659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294653#post1294653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Lunar turns into a bird and flies away in a flock, she gets a great view of the tribe she was training being slaughtered, her demesne overrun, and gets to hear her wife and kids being taken away in chains.<br /> <br /> Congrats, Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>But she lives to fight another day, revengeance and all that rot. Or yeah she could just Kamikaze too... I\u2019m sure that\u2019s satisfying in its own regard.<br /> <br /> Also you have utter bastard Lunars who view their children and worshipers as disposable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:39:03-08:00","id":1294660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294654#post1294654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 7? I thought it was five.<br /> <br /> Yurgen Kaneko, the 2nd-highest-essence Dawn in Creation<br /> Samea, the highest-essence Zenith in Creation, and the most powerful sorcerer amongst the Solars<br /> Fear-Eater, Eclipse Shaman<br /> Nalla Bloodaxe, Night Caste<br /> A Twilight whose name I forget.<br /> <br /> They didn't have a Tear Eater army though, they had an Icewalker army of Tiger Warriors (though I assume they call them Mammoth warriors or something, not many Tigers up north), and some demons.<br /> In 2nd ed, also Haltans, Ourcastes and Warstriders, but I don't believe that's still the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a good point I guess they would Call then Mammoth Warriors or Berzerkers, or Ulfhednar.<br /> <br /> They also had the backing of two Golden Lions, at least one 2nd Circle Demon, and Animal Avatars/Fathers/Mother\u2019s like The Great Mammoth who sent its children to aid in crucial battles.<br /> <br /> But it was an interesting conflict. Surely we have Chejop and others attesting feeding the Tepet Legions to the Bull (in earlier editions it was so confusing figuring out the difference between realm and House Legions so I am so happy they cleared it out with 3rd ed), but Perhaps the Sidereals were Hoping for a Pyrrhic victory, so the Tepet would be Crippled but the North Tamed. I\u2019m sure the Empress was more pragmatic then the Sidereals concerning whether they won or lost, she knew it was a bleak corner of the World and she could afford the sacrifice as it was more important to humble her proudest children, while the Bronze Faction doesn\u2019t like losing resources just as a favor to the pompous Queen of the Mortal Universe, they probably were expecting to tame the North and create a foothold of Civilization more open to their secret influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:39:20-08:00","id":1294661,"title":"","content":"So. This thread is basically swinging between &quot;The wyld hunt is an extremely potent and motivated institution with a lot of resources and a lot of expertise in dealing with just about everything any exalt has ever thrown at them&quot; and &quot;yes but there's this one trick....&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to admit a perfect wyld hunt, you can't.<br /> If you want to admit a perfect getaway from the hunt, you'll be talking at, tops, 3 or 4 lunars in the entire world. The hunt has 396 other lunars to worry about.<br /> <br /> You also underestimate exalts as a whole, apparently.<br /> Sidereals as as much cheaters as lunars, and if it's about hunting down one of the trickier lunars you can expect a sidereal to be watching over the hunt.<br /> Sometimes you come down to &quot;but can they even murder everything at once in a second?&quot; the answer is <b><i>yes</i></b>. There's plenty aoe, infinite-ish multiattacks and the like with DBs and the things they can afford.<br /> Sometimes you come down to &quot;but sometimes it's really easy to just get away&quot;. Sense-riding Technique is Essence 3 and at the end of a great chain of charms, absolutely something you should expect from a hunting party.<br /> <br /> You also underestimate too much the wyld hunt destroying everything the lunar was building. Generally if a lunar is being suspected he already overcommitted. Without going into builds that maybe two lunars in the entire Creation can pull off, any given lunar is just one mistake away from being skewered by a dozen dragonbloods and a small army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:40:41-08:00","id":1294662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294656#post1294656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Siberian (Haslantian maybe, my Exalted geography/real world analogues isn't great) tigers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah that\u2019s also a good point! Sure we do have subarctic tigers so they definitely have them! As well as Sabertooth Tigers! So Sabertooth Tiger Warriors it is for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:45:51-08:00","id":1294663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294658#post1294658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mate the only thing close to a goalpost/thesis I believe I made was that Wyld Hunts need to either have a solid Ambush or get the Lunars to initiate a Last Stand Protocol. Everything else all the discussions they are open to change. The whole point of this thread is discussion, it isn\u2019t even a debate.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll note this thread would have been worthwhile just from the posts of Dr. Lovemonkey and Brilliantrain, they had excellent insight and they posted in a manner that inspired several ideas I want to try in a game.<br /> And even Slarn who provided counterpoints to my ideas seems to be enjoying the thread, sorry if I came off as uncool, I reread some of my replies and they may seem that way I appreciate your involvement in the discussion. And even the singular things have been useful like Heavyarms pointing out that Earth aspect tidbit or alucard talking about spells like DoOBs.<br /> <br /> Your coming at this like your trying to \u201cwin\u201d something and I\u2019m stating that is not the point of the thread. I will continue to point out hypotheticals if I find them useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294628#post1294628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not moving goal posts, Lunars often Lair in caves and serious wilderness. If you have ever lived even remotely in the country you would know it\u2019s trivially easy to scare any nearby cluster of birds, it\u2019s a simple stunt and one the Lunar would cultivate rather easy if so inclined and even if they weren\u2019t it\u2019s a consequence of living in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> What do you honestly consider a general circumstance? Do your view in Lunars have them all live in a village or small town? The vast majority of Lunars that I have read that have mentioned their homes involves them lairing in distant manses or deep wild areas, Gerd Marrow Eater, Lilith, Magnificent Jaguar.<br /> <br /> What do you consider a general Lunar home? Is it an apartment in Nexus? Maybe if the Lunar is wearing someone\u2019s skin...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s weighed in Favor if Lunars because Lunars don\u2019t Sleep under Bridges with giant moonsilver signs saying don\u2019t ambush me I\u2019m sleeping, and if they did it\u2019s probably a trap.<br /> <br /> <br /> No seriously what do you consider a suitable general Lunar home?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was your response when I questioned your response initially with the bats.<br /> <br /> How is that not suggesting that the attack needs to be against the lunar home? Seriously is anyone else able to point out to me how? Because I genuinely just don't get how I can interpret this any other way.<br /> <br /> I didn't come in to win. I was just pointing out much little mechanical weight being tiny actually gives you. Yet you jumped on with your contrived circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:50:03-08:00","id":1294665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294657#post1294657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A foolish mistake.. trusting people?<br /> <br /> El, it really sounds like you're arguing from the conclusion rather than the inverse. You're starting with the thesis than Lunars are hard to capture, and then concocting plans to justify it. They are difficult. But you're reaching here<br /> <br /> If you don't have anyone who can sense a Lunars tell, you are thorough when purging, and kill every animal they <i>might </i>be. While miniscule sized shapes are problematic, environmental attacks like flooding the place or fire and smoke should make it hard to keep them up. Maybe you miss them. If you do, the Hunt probably returns to civilization and remains for a bit in case the Lunar pops up again nearby<br /> <br /> Demons and spirits are not akin to omniscience. Plus they're enemies Shikari are going to be really good against due to the Immaculate Styles. <br /> <br /> If the Realm are in a position to 'corner' a Lunar, they've got supply lines and local resources. And you're right. It's going to be really hard to ambush a Lunar in their lair. So you either encircle the lair, or set a trap elsewhere. If you're fighting the Lunar head to head with battle groups and a Wyld Hunt, it's much harder to get away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am spreading wide net with my shotgun approach of strategies. But I stand by it. Lunars aren\u2019t limited to standing in the middle of the room and declaring they are going to turn into a Rhino or Eagle, they are going to be clever.<br /> <br /> And yes as I pointed out you have to raise the geographical region if you want to make sure the Lunar you Lost track of is dead, meanwhile there is a significant moral loss if you can\u2019t gaurantee a victory with a Corpse, they may say they won but people will have doubts eating at them. Also Gods are not all going to be cheering you on as you genocide all life in a forest, burn it down and then flood it, yeah some gods will cheer but they will be probably be considered Jackasses by the locals. In general that amount of chaos and slaughter earns the Ire of many spirits. Do it often, especially without a pelt to show for it and you might have a official complaints Piling up with the Censor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also how many powers do Lunars have to Fake their death this time around? Is that a thing? I feel like that should be a thing... the Fera did it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:51:56-08:00","id":1294666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294654#post1294654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7? I thought it was five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its 6, you forgot Crimson Antler. All we know about them is that they're <b>another</b> Icewalker Solar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294653#post1294653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Lunar turns into a bird and flies away in a flock, she gets a great view of the tribe she was training being slaughtered, her demesne overrun, and gets to hear her wife and kids being taken away in chains.<br /> <br /> Congrats, Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think two Bronze Faction Sidereals would high five over this outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:58:06-08:00","id":1294667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294663#post1294663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHmm..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That was your response when I questioned your response initially with the bats.<br /> <br /> How is that not suggesting that the attack needs to be against the lunar home? Seriously is anyone else able to point out to me how? Because I genuinely just don't get how I can interpret this any other way.<br /> <br /> I didn't come in to win. I was just pointing out much little mechanical weight being tiny actually gives you. Yet you jumped on with your contrived circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>? I was talking about attacking their Lair because that was the example scenario we were already discussing? How is that moving the goal post?<br /> <br /> Tiny gives you a lot of options, it\u2019s not as simple as pressing the tiny Button and you tiny at them. That is why we now have that charm, What was it Tyrant Mouse something, that allows you to shrink in size. Stunts, cover and a boatload of tactical significance goes with it. Take for Example those Cenotes in Mexico, you get in a tangle there if you shrink they need to constantly rearrange the stone to get to you or bring the whole place down, but if you have the right forms you can survive a cave in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:08:11-08:00","id":1294668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294661#post1294661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. This thread is basically swinging between &amp;quot;The wyld hunt is an extremely potent and motivated institution with a lot of resources and a lot of expertise in dealing with just about everything any exalt has ever thrown at them&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;yes but there's this one trick....&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to admit a perfect wyld hunt, you can't.<br /> If you want to admit a perfect getaway from the hunt, you'll be talking at, tops, 3 or 4 lunars in the entire world. The hunt has 396 other lunars to worry about.<br /> <br /> You also underestimate exalts as a whole, apparently.<br /> Sidereals as as much cheaters as lunars, and if it's about hunting down one of the trickier lunars you can expect a sidereal to be watching over the hunt.<br /> Sometimes you come down to &amp;quot;but can they even murder everything at once in a second?&amp;quot; the answer is <b><i>yes</i></b>. There's plenty aoe, infinite-ish multiattacks and the like with DBs and the things they can afford.<br /> Sometimes you come down to &amp;quot;but sometimes it's really easy to just get away&amp;quot;. Sense-riding Technique is Essence 3 and at the end of a great chain of charms, absolutely something you should expect from a hunting party.<br /> <br /> You also underestimate too much the wyld hunt destroying everything the lunar was building. Generally if a lunar is being suspected he already overcommitted. Without going into builds that maybe two lunars in the entire Creation can pull off, any given lunar is just one mistake away from being skewered by a dozen dragonbloods and a small army.</div> </div> </div> </div>In pretty sure there are more then 4 Lunars in Creation who can escape from a well prepared Wyld Hunt. All I\u2019m saying is unless they really nail the contingencies and preparation there is always a reasonable chance the Lunar can escape if they are not suicidal.<br /> <br /> You say I underestimate the Wyld Hunt burning down their plans and genociding their loved ones, that doesn\u2019t make it true. I say I\u2019m estimating them. If they are on the Rim of Creation and have a full blown culture that can defend themselves it\u2019s going to be a helluva an expensive Wyld Hunt to travel thousands of miles from the the threshold to Genocide a Civilization that can fight back and wipe out their secret beast master. It more viable if it\u2019s within the Threshold, the farther from the Inland sea the more the odds are stacked against you if you want to Hannibal genocide a whole people. That\u2019s a different. Argument then just assassinating a Lunar. If your assuming they have a people\u2019s they are working on it complicates things, unless it\u2019s just a small clan or tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:09:26-08:00","id":1294669,"title":"","content":"This threads too engaging! I needed to slumber hours ago rather then read and type on my phone all night! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> G\u2019night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:17:28-08:00","id":1294671,"title":"","content":"If they are on the rim of creation they're reduced to near irrelevancy.<br /> Having a chance to escape does not mean having a nearly guaranteed way to escape, and overall you are treating the latter as far closer to the former than it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:19:06-08:00","id":1294672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294667#post1294667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ? I was talking about attacking their Lair because that was the example scenario we were already discussing? How is that moving the goal post?<br /> <br /> Tiny gives you a lot of options, it\u2019s not as simple as pressing the tiny Button and you tiny at them. That is why we now have that charm, What was it Tyrant Mouse something, that allows you to shrink in size. Stunts, cover and a boatload of tactical significance goes with it. Take for Example those Cenotes in Mexico, you get in a tangle there if you shrink they need to constantly rearrange the stone to get to you or bring the whole place down, but if you have the right forms you can survive a cave in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes tiny gives advantages. But if you are already in combat it is not helping you disengage. It will help you establish surprise and go to ground. However you still need to succeed at stealth. Also even when in stealth you still need to succeed at disengage when at close range. Which circumstances won't always be in your favour. It certainly helps though and even the clumsiest of lunars should succeed against most mortals. Just once dragon blooded are thrown in the mix it is not a certainty.<br /> <br /> Looking back yes you introduced that the attack was on the lunars lair earlier. But funnily enough Isator called you on that when you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:17:47-08:00","id":1294681,"title":"","content":"I would just like to point out the way Sidereal Dodge works, means that a Sidereal who feels sneaky might elect to ride out with the Dragon-Blooded to meet their Anathema foe, Join Battle against the Lunar, let the Lunar <i>start</i> escaping, use Avoidance Kata, and start directing the reserves to where the Lunar is going, so as to catch her in a pincer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-07-2019, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:32:31-08:00","id":1294686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294656#post1294656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Siberian (Haslantian maybe, my Exalted geography/real world analogues isn't great) tigers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure where Siberian Tigers should go in Exalted.<br /> I used to live east of the Mongolian steppe, and my city had a reservation with 300 Siberian Tigers, so I think they live more near the steppe than up in the arctic parts of Siberia. Subarctic, as Eldagusto said. I assume they need big flat areas rather than coastal areas, so probably not Haslanti, as the Haslanti cities are built by the mountains near the coast. Maybe more the northeast forests? I'm no expert on tigers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:35:46-08:00","id":1294687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294666#post1294666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its 6, you forgot Crimson Antler. All we know about them is that they're <b>another</b> Icewalker Solar.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think two Bronze Faction Sidereals would high five over this outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably a Solar. There was that mention in Infernals, and Crimson Antler is the only one to never get a write-up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:37:22-08:00","id":1294689,"title":"","content":"You know, I could just about tolerate the general formats of the replies, but the numbers of &quot;mates&quot; and &quot;brohams&quot; and similar little condescensions make the topic feel distinctly uninviting to engage with.<br /> <br /> Besides, I find that everybody else has effectively answered the question in various facets to the satisfaction of one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:01:31-08:00","id":1294699,"title":"","content":"If anything this topic has made me.more convinced Lunars are pretty well balanced because there is a lot of 'well a Lunar can maybe escape' and a lot of 'well a Wyld hunt might be prepared for that'.<br /> <br /> It makes it feel like the main thing determining success or failure is each group's information gathering, which is something exceptional for Exalted, since it helps make an atmosphere of a game where you really want to consider your actions before you do them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:07:41-08:00","id":1294701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294699#post1294699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything this topic has made me.more convinced Lunars are pretty well balanced because there is a lot of 'well a Lunar can maybe escape' and a lot of 'well a Wyld hunt might be prepared for that'.<br /> <br /> It makes it feel like the main thing determining success or failure is each group's information gathering, which is something exceptional for Exalted, since it helps make an atmosphere of a game where you really want to consider your actions before you do them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t forget resources and good old fashioned luck either. Allies, by way of loyalty or mercenary or diplomacy, and artifacts and all that matter, and even with them it\u2019s hard to be 100% sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:30:15-08:00","id":1294714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294689#post1294689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, I find that everybody else has effectively answered the question in various facets to the satisfaction of one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like it to me too.<br /> <br /> Lunars are tricksy.<br /> Sidereals are also tricksy.<br /> Lunars are masters of asymmetric warfare.<br /> Dragonblood can engage in all the traditional tactics of an Empire facing asymmetric warfare.*<br /> A pack of 4-5 Lunars is extremely powerful.<br /> There are loads of Dragonblood to face them.<br /> Lunars are really good at spying on incoming Dragonblood.<br /> Sidereals and some Dragonblood are also good at spying.<br /> <br /> So, basically, you can't really say that Lunars are always going to win or Dragonblood are always going to win.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Any Brits on here hear Rees-Mogg on TV defending the time we invented concentration camps to put Boer women and children in, where most of them starved or died of disease? What a pleasure it is to have him fighting the Brexit fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2019, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:07:50-08:00","id":1294762,"title":"","content":"Beat to death, but I still want to comment on this.<br /> How does a Wyld Hunt corner Lunars?<br /> Depends on what the Wyld Hunt is supposed to be doing in the first place. <br /> New Lunar? (And there has to be some success in hunting new Lunars, otherwise there would only be old Lunars.) Since it is a race between the Silver Pact and the Wyld Hunt as to who gets to the new lunar first, I would guess the Hunt has a pretty good record of nailing newbies. (Also look at the 3e released fiction of Seven Devil Clever to see how the Hunt might operate.)<br /> Older Lunar? The Lunar must be doing something to attract the Realm's attention. Which means something is going on that the Realm wants stopped. Which means stopping whatever it is is the Hunt's goal, and bagging the Lunar is gravy. Older Lunars will more than likely escape, but at the cost of the Realm showing that it has power to control this area. Unless the Lunar's idea is to drag the Wyld Hunt all over Creation (and then they have to just get away, and still be able to be found, or the Hunt goes home), the Hunt has foiled whatever plot the Lunar was cooking up.<br /> And, in fact, a 1e story had a Dragonblooded looking at the opening of yet another battle with the Lunar Anathema, Sleeves of War (with whom he has personally crossed blades with at least once). Meaning that there has been several battles, and since the DB has survived them, I would speculate that most were Realm victories, with Sleeves of War using Lunar tricks to escape and raise another army. So yes, Lunars can escape after losing. But the Realm keeps winning battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:02:22-08:00","id":1294813,"title":"","content":"In many ways that\u2019s the Silver Pact modus operandi: let the Realm \u201cwin,\u201d but only in the most expensive way possible and make sure you escape afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:11:18-08:00","id":1294816,"title":"","content":"Your average Lunar PC is going to beat your average Wyld Hunt to death. The Wyld Hunt is one of those things (like the Realm generally) that never actually succeeds at much of anything; it's billed as a threat but is built in such a way that it's often trivially easy for celestial PCs to out fight/out think/out magic/etc.<br /> <br /> The setting conceit that the weakest exalts in the setting somehow have their collective boot on the world hangs by a thread; it's probably best not to pick at that thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:20:22-08:00","id":1294820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294816#post1294816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your average Lunar PC is going to beat your average Wyld Hunt to death. The Wyld Hunt is one of those things (like the Realm generally) that never actually succeeds at much of anything; it's billed as a threat but is built in such a way that it's often trivially easy for celestial PCs to out fight/out think/out magic/etc.<br /> <br /> The setting conceit that the weakest exalts in the setting somehow have their collective boot on the world hangs by a thread; it's probably best not to pick at that thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your average group of Lunar PCs will absoluely beat an average Wyld Hunt to death. Because that's not what your average Wyld Hunt is designed to do.<br /> <br /> 1 Lunar PC with, say, 0-100xp? With a 2/3rds chance of not being a Full Moon?<br /> <br /> 7 Essence 3 Dragonblood and 100 soldiers will, if the Lunar doesn't flee, probably kill the Lunar. 1 attack a turn, enhanced by Lunar charms, is going to do way less damage than 7 attacks, enhanced by Dragonblood charms. They'll mote-tap the Lunar quickly, probably throw a ton of Overwhelming penalties on them, then butcher them. They may be so overwhelmed (losing motes and initiative defending themselves) that they may not even kill a single Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:27:01-08:00","id":1294827,"title":"","content":"I think even your average group of Lunar PCs at chargen wouldn\u2019t stand up well to that. If you\u2019ve got a circle of three, one of each caste, they\u2019re still outnumbered by more than 2 to 1, and with charms like Harnessed Firestorm Onslaught And Deadly Wildfire Legion, that\u2019s pretty dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:33:30-08:00","id":1294830,"title":"","content":"Problem with these scenario threads is that the lone Celestial always comes across as a player character with a permissive Storyteller.<br /> &quot;I turn into a bird and fly away&quot; &quot;yes, the five Dragon-Blooded shake their fists impotently at you as you make your escape&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T12:44:55-08:00","id":1294837,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no Dragonblood ever uses Elemental Bolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:03:46-08:00","id":1294847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294659#post1294659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But she lives to fight another day, revengeance and all that rot. Or yeah she could just Kamikaze too... I\u2019m sure that\u2019s satisfying in its own regard.<br /> <br /> Also you have utter bastard Lunars who view their children and worshipers as disposable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all true. But you asked how the Wyld Hunt could ever kill a Lunar, not how the Wyld Hunt would kill every single Lunar.<br /> <br /> And even utter bastards might start questioning their running away protocols if their family and ambitions were constantly being wiped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:13:25-08:00","id":1294853,"title":"","content":"Turnabout is about fair. Lunars can also hunt.<br /> <br /> There is a couple of lunars that have this modus operandi: one of them is bait, making an 'easy' target for the wyld hunt. She is an expert in creating just enough trouble to get the wyld hunt coming, but not really enough to justify a sideral assassin (there are a handful of these available at any time). Let's call her Target.<br /> <br /> When the wyld hunt comes, the lunar 'dies', with help of Ebon Shadow and such trickery (it seems that Lunars have other fake-death effects on the Stamina preview today). One of the shikari suggests very convincingly to burn the unholy corpse (which Target survives, due to her Stamina Charms, but she looks very convincingly burned), and take its artifacts (which the lunar didn't have, such bad luck!). The shikari that gave the idea is Face, a lunar that took place of one of the shikaris while all attention was on Target. Face returns to the Wyld Hunt regional quarters. A little of Manipulation paranoia effects later (Lunar Manipulation Charms make The Thing look like a walk on the park), Face leaves with most of the shikari killing each other, and she and Target clean house. They leave quarters are loaded with artifacts. Such profit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:17:24-08:00","id":1294856,"title":"","content":"Ok? <br /> <br /> The dragon blooded, using awareness charms and cooperative charms and spells like sworn brotherhood and ten thousand dragons fight as one.<br /> <br /> They realize that a foul anathema has infiltrated their group and kill him. Target tries to flee, but is taken down by a hail of a dozen elemental arrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:20:56-08:00","id":1294857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294681#post1294681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just like to point out the way Sidereal Dodge works, means that a Sidereal who feels sneaky might elect to ride out with the Dragon-Blooded to meet their Anathema foe, Join Battle against the Lunar, let the Lunar <i>start</i> escaping, use Avoidance Kata, and start directing the reserves to where the Lunar is going, so as to catch her in a pincer.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t know exactly how Sidereal Dodge works yet though, aren\u2019t you one of the biggest proponents of we can\u2019t trust older editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:24:30-08:00","id":1294858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294689#post1294689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I could just about tolerate the general formats of the replies, but the numbers of &amp;quot;mates&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;brohams&amp;quot; and similar little condescensions make the topic feel distinctly uninviting to engage with.<br /> <br /> Besides, I find that everybody else has effectively answered the question in various facets to the satisfaction of one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you prefer good sir? I\u2019ve said mate and broham regularly since before this was even the Onxy path Forum. If you don\u2019t like the thread don\u2019t engage with it, or I don\u2019t know try to get it shut down or something, you do you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:31:23-08:00","id":1294859,"title":"","content":"So... is broham, like, a brother who's quite hammy?<br /> Or is it just like Broseph and Broseiden?<br /> <br /> I haven't heard it before.<br /> <br /> (I also think it's worth noting that this is a multinational forum, and while &quot;mate&quot; and &quot;bro&quot; might sound, without being able to see expressions, somewhat condescending, and &quot;good sir&quot; extremely hostile, to those of us from certain nations, in other nations it probably sounds polite and friendly.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:32:41-08:00","id":1294861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294813#post1294813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many ways that\u2019s the Silver Pact modus operandi: let the Realm \u201cwin,\u201d but only in the most expensive way possible and make sure you escape afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s impression I got. It\u2019s costly to hold territory the Realm wants, and mostly the Caul will be were you get those kind of disputes, but everywhere else is about dragging as much resource talent and attrition from the realm as you can. If you conquer a territory you have to defend it, if you think the realm is going to win anyways make them work for the squeeze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:39:35-08:00","id":1294866,"title":"","content":"Looking through Seven Devil Clever's story, I see she was only chased by 3 immaculates. Think about what it would have been like in the days before the Empress vanished and the Wyld Hunt was supported. How many dragonblooded would there have been then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:44:52-08:00","id":1294868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294830#post1294830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with these scenario threads is that the lone Celestial always comes across as a player character with a permissive Storyteller.<br /> &amp;quot;I turn into a bird and fly away&amp;quot; &amp;quot;yes, the five Dragon-Blooded shake their fists impotently at you as you make your escape&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Do you think that might be a bit of an oversimplification or strawman of the discussion? We have brought up artifact charm back archery, and spells as well as various complications that may arise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously would people be stomping their foot down so much about this if the title of the thread was something like Sell me on The Wyld Hunt succeeding against Lunars?<br /> <br /> Like ten pages is good for a discussion, I can see people just not commenting after they made their peace but to crap on the basic desire to to even make this thread in the first place...? What the Hell should people discuss on a forum. Is it a forbidden topic to even discuss this? We are in Lunar Kickstarter Month it only makes sense to bring this up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T14:31:14-08:00","id":1294883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294820#post1294820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 Essence 3 Dragonblood and 100 soldiers</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, we've seen two Wyld Hunts in the 3E text, and neither looked like that. One hunt got clowned by a noob solar, and the other scored a temporary, arguably Pyrrhic, victory after being massacred by two Lunars on the first go (and that was decades ago when, so I'm told, the Wyld Hunt was less inept and ineffectual.).<br /> <br /> I'd very much appreciate sources in the text to the contrary, as none immediately come to my mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T15:18:30-08:00","id":1294894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294883#post1294883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, we've seen two Wyld Hunts in the 3E text, and neither looked like that. One hunt got clowned by a noob solar, and the other scored a temporary, arguably Pyrrhic, victory after being massacred by two Lunars on the first go (and that was decades ago when, so I'm told, the Wyld Hunt was less inept and ineffectual.).<br /> <br /> I'd very much appreciate sources in the text to the contrary, as none immediately come to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? The opening Hunt for the book is exactly like that. The dead number so many that River's hands ache from writing all of the condolence letters. That's more than a handful of soldiers, and they also mention monks. Her Hunt failed because they were not acting as one. They were even about to receive reenforcements in the form of more soldiers, before the other two DBs showed up. Then they went 5v2 with no mortal backup, killed one and did the even more impressive task of taking the other prisoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T15:20:05-08:00","id":1294895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294534#post1294534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just remember, Dynasts have been training to deal with problems like this since they've been children, and some have the experience of centuries behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now convinced that if The Realm doesn't feature a number of childhood games inspired by hunting Lunars, it has half-failed as a document because it hasn't explored the logical conclusion of a culture whose primary enemy are shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Imagine the variations on games of hide and seek, and games of tag, where certain players have subtle ribbons or tokens included in their clothes, or scales painted on a part of their body, and everyone else has to find the marked player who is trying to hide among the other players who are also trying to hide.<br /> <br /> Games of telephone, which start with how information becomes twisted through natural, honest repetition, and then evolves into games of information control.<br /> <br /> Card games like that &quot;secret fascist&quot; thing my coworker talks about, where one player is the hidden enemy and pretends to be a normal player while passing evil legislation and turning other players against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T15:31:47-08:00","id":1294900,"title":"","content":"Ooh that's good. I've also recently been introduced to the idea of skill gates as keys. Basically instead of a password you need to flawlessly execute some difficult task to prove your identity. That way even if the info is somehow extracted from you, the skill isn't immediately transferable. I can only imagine the insane greetings or literal secret handshakes that get developed as they grow up. <br /> <br /> <br /> Dynast 1: &quot;Hey! Dynast 2! How's that peach of the reef?&quot; Holding out hand Palm down<br /> <br /> Dynast 2: &quot;Oh, you know, it's tastey still.&quot; Awkwardly batting at the underside of Dynast 1s hand<br /> <br /> Dynast 1 instantly draws her daiklave &quot;You will pay for killing my sister.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> And epic Kung fu fight ensues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:17:07-08:00","id":1294937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294857#post1294857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don\u2019t know exactly how Sidereal Dodge works yet though\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026but we know Avoidance Kata is still going to be a thing. The example Sidereal in the Core has it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294857#post1294857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026aren\u2019t you one of the biggest proponents of we can\u2019t trust older editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hardly a black and white issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:46:55-08:00","id":1294946,"title":"","content":"avoidance kata is so iconic that I'll be immensely surprised if they removed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T20:49:30-08:00","id":1294964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294681#post1294681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just like to point out the way Sidereal Dodge works, means that a Sidereal who feels sneaky might elect to ride out with the Dragon-Blooded to meet their Anathema foe, Join Battle against the Lunar, let the Lunar <i>start</i> escaping, use Avoidance Kata, and start directing the reserves to where the Lunar is going, so as to catch her in a pincer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Avoidance Kata like that is slightly unpredictable, since you don't get to pick where you end up - the only real guarantee (and even that is not 100%) is that it's safe and somewhere you plausibly could have gone instead. While that's <i>probably</i> someplace you can direct your forces from, it's not certain.<br /> <br /> I suspect that if you're sending a Sidereal after a Lunar, what they often do is drop an astrological curse on them that makes them easier to find and pursue in the future, which makes it harder for them to escape, or which otherwise acts to corner them, since those are very hard to shake off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T21:09:27-08:00","id":1294967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294883#post1294883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, we've seen two Wyld Hunts in the 3E text, and neither looked like that. One hunt got clowned by a noob solar, and the other scored a temporary, arguably Pyrrhic, victory after being massacred by two Lunars on the first go (and that was decades ago when, so I'm told, the Wyld Hunt was less inept and ineffectual.).<br /> <br /> I'd very much appreciate sources in the text to the contrary, as none immediately come to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>DrLoveMonkey pointed out the extremely well-supported hunt in the beginning of WFHW which failed... and the 5v2 fight that goes way better when the Dragonblooded involved actually bother to fight like Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Because DBs ain't the Mook Exalted in 3e, they are merely the least individually powerful ones. So they try very hard to not fight as individuals, if they wish success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T01:04:25-08:00","id":1294992,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think it would be useful to consider more concrete examples, take it out of the white room as it were!<br /> <br /> From the top of my head a Wyld Hunt might be called to deal with either a newly exalted Lunar, one which is reported harassing a region (so, not a newby) or to assault an entrenched Lunar (likely an elder). For the first your team is whomever is closest, the second will be more prepared and the last, well, that's more a full-blown military operation.<br /> <br /> In any case, the DB's will not be going in blind and clueless. They will investigate. Scenes will be cased, witnesses canvassed and the Lunar profiled. Very handy for figuring the Tell and more. They should have an idea of its capabilities, powers, objective and preferred tactics. In other words, they can prepare. If you can figure out what it's after, lure it out and lay traps. If it's prone to flying away, have Agatae ready to materialize and pounce on it. Birds aren't the best forms to slug it out, you see. If it relies on disappearing among other animals, prepare area attacks. If it's the scary type or reliant on messing with your mind, do team building exercises, get to know each other intimately and use your magic to bolster your courage. Prepare workings or spirits with the sole purpose of spotting the Lunar, marking it visibly, or tracking it. Use poison. If you can figure out if the Lunar has allies or people they care about, stake them out, or take them hostage and use them against it.<br /> <br /> In other words, first gather intelligence so you can formulate a real plan to counter whatever tricks the filthy Anathema has up its sleeve. The Dragonblooded's toolbox of tricks of their own is just about as large as that of the Lunars, so don't just blunder blindly into a fight hoping it will somehow work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T03:53:32-08:00","id":1295006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294868#post1294868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Do you think that might be a bit of an oversimplification or strawman of the discussion? We have brought up artifact charm back archery, and spells as well as various complications that may arise.</div> </div> </div> </div>No comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seriously would people be stomping their foot down so much about this if the title of the thread was something like Sell me on The Wyld Hunt succeeding against Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div> It would've given them a better idea of what they were in for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like ten pages is good for a discussion, I can see people just not commenting after they made their peace but to crap on the basic desire to to even make this thread in the first place...? What the Hell should people discuss on a forum. Is it a forbidden topic to even discuss this? We are in Lunar Kickstarter Month it only makes sense to bring this up.</div> </div> </div> </div> People are getting annoyed with you. Is that because you've challenged some forum orthodoxy or is it because you're being dismissive and rude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:11:14-08:00","id":1295062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295006#post1295006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No comment.<br /> <br /> It would've given them a better idea of what they were in for.<br /> <br /> People are getting annoyed with you. Is that because you've challenged some forum orthodoxy or is it because you're being dismissive and rude?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have incorporated what a lot of people said into the discussion, and it\u2019s even given me a more comfortable view of the Wyld Hunt. I do not have any regrets because some people don\u2019t like me using words like mate, or because I don\u2019t roll over and show my throat. We are supposed to be adults, it\u2019s okay that people disagree, and there is no need to stomp ones foot over and over to get me to agree on specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:13:15-08:00","id":1295064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294967#post1294967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DrLoveMonkey pointed out the extremely well-supported hunt in the beginning of WFHW which failed... and the 5v2 fight that goes way better when the Dragonblooded involved actually bother to fight like Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Because DBs ain't the Mook Exalted in 3e, they are merely the least individually powerful ones. So they try very hard to not fight as individuals, if they wish success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they also got renewed by two fresh members and they pressed their advantage against the Solar and Lunar that seemed to be injured and tired from round one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:18:14-08:00","id":1295066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294992#post1294992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think it would be useful to consider more concrete examples, take it out of the white room as it were!<br /> <br /> From the top of my head a Wyld Hunt might be called to deal with either a newly exalted Lunar, one which is reported harassing a region (so, not a newby) or to assault an entrenched Lunar (likely an elder). For the first your team is whomever is closest, the second will be more prepared and the last, well, that's more a full-blown military operation.<br /> <br /> In any case, the DB's will not be going in blind and clueless. They will investigate. Scenes will be cased, witnesses canvassed and the Lunar profiled. Very handy for figuring the Tell and more. They should have an idea of its capabilities, powers, objective and preferred tactics. In other words, they can prepare. If you can figure out what it's after, lure it out and lay traps. If it's prone to flying away, have Agatae ready to materialize and pounce on it. Birds aren't the best forms to slug it out, you see. If it relies on disappearing among other animals, prepare area attacks. If it's the scary type or reliant on messing with your mind, do team building exercises, get to know each other intimately and use your magic to bolster your courage. Prepare workings or spirits with the sole purpose of spotting the Lunar, marking it visibly, or tracking it. Use poison. If you can figure out if the Lunar has allies or people they care about, stake them out, or take them hostage and use them against it.<br /> <br /> In other words, first gather intelligence so you can formulate a real plan to counter whatever tricks the filthy Anathema has up its sleeve. The Dragonblooded's toolbox of tricks of their own is just about as large as that of the Lunars, so don't just blunder blindly into a fight hoping it will somehow work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably closest to how I would handle it in game.<br /> <br /> Again can anyone answer my question about if Lunars stay in the form they were in when they die or if they revert to some base form?<br /> <br /> And if you area of effect a local how do you know you killed the Lunar especially if they use a play dead trick like Ebon Shadow style and are buried in rubble or ash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:30:56-08:00","id":1295079,"title":"","content":"So a thing to note on the discussion vis a vis the Wyld Hunt's we have listed. From the looks of it the first Wyld Hunt in WFHW. First River notes that Eshuvar joined in a few months after leaving the Heptagram, so from a character gen perspective he's a newbie. We don't get a timescale for how long River has been active and River speculates that Swift probably isn't more than 12 years into her service. So if we were to try and say this maps to character gen rules as opposed to narrative, these three were low xp if not flat out new characters. <br /> <br /> The strategy was also described as, &quot; A show of Immaculate force&quot; so its entirely possible that the strategy was lacking and consisted of drawing the Anathema to the bulk of the forces and killing them there. I'll also note it appears the only dead were mortals as no one mentions any deceased DBs and I feel like it would have been mentioned if any more DBs had been killed in the fighting. So it sounds like the battle had the Anathema focusing on mortal casulaties and just general havoc as opposed to engaging the DBs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:50:09-08:00","id":1295082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1294967#post1294967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DrLoveMonkey pointed out the extremely well-supported hunt in the beginning of WFHW which failed... and the 5v2 fight that goes way better when the Dragonblooded involved actually bother to fight like Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Because DBs ain't the Mook Exalted in 3e, they are merely the least individually powerful ones. So they try very hard to not fight as individuals, if they wish success.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to understand an unknown number of people as at least 100 soldiers, though I'm not sure why. Further, they 5v2 (after having several DBs killed) kill one and capture the other... who later escapes (after we find the most of the five have lived fairly unfulfilling lives in the meantime).<br /> <br /> That's the height of DB success in 3E; I'm not quite impressed by their prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:25:46-08:00","id":1295091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295082#post1295082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to understand an unknown number of people as at least 100 soldiers, though I'm not sure why.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you seem determined to interpret everything in the worst light possible, and interject it everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further, they 5v2 (after having several DBs killed) kill one and capture the other... who later escapes</div> </div> </div> </div>That escape is not on them.<br /> <br /> They delivered a living and subdued Solar Exalt before the Scarlet Empress, to be taken off into the Imperial Manse for whatever bizarre experiments. The general framing of the setting presents that as a feat of renown even among the Wyld Hunt. That he was kept alive long enough, for <i>decades</i>, that the improbable disappearance of the Empress that absolutely nobody predicted allowed him to escape, is rather out of their hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(after we find the most of the five have lived fairly unfulfilling lives in the meantime).</div> </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the height of DB success in 3E</div> </div> </div> </div>The height of Dragon Blooded success in Third Edition is the Realm. Broken down then into the kinds of feats ascribed to the Great Houses, such as Ragara's secret experiments, or Ledaal arming itself for war against the Deathlords, or Peleps being so huge that they could plausibly break off and turn the West into their own separate empire with blackjack and hookers. Further devolved into the innumerable feats ascribed to individual sample characters in the House write-ups and Artifact backstories. You find nothing impressive in the feat of Cathak Falu in creating Pyre of Legions, or Peleps Lirel for Sea's Verdict? <br /> <br /> That's without even getting into all of the neat stuff ascribed to various classes of outcaste. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite impressed by their prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, what would impress you?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:05:27-08:00","id":1295101,"title":"","content":"Oh boy now with the off topic bickering.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways back on subject. I remember in older books they downplayed Wyldhunts against non Solars, and Wyld Hunts seemed to be more a pageantry filled show of force against baby Solars, with maybe only a couple of Wyld Hunts a a year on a busy year, depending on how frequently the Solars rehosted. With very minimal emphasis on hunting new Lunars, with that more of an occasional thing that sometimes caught their eye. Now by 3rd ed I get the impression of a much more active Wyld Hunt, that seems to be popping Hunts off left and right, yet at the same time they take note of things Like Mnemon calling out the other houses for not backing more Hunts.<br /> <br /> Before I got an impression they rarely if ever had multiple Hunts on at one time, until the Scarlet Empress disappeared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:19:03-08:00","id":1295105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295082#post1295082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to understand an unknown number of people as at least 100 soldiers, though I'm not sure why. Further, they 5v2 (after having several DBs killed) kill one and capture the other... who later escapes (after we find the most of the five have lived fairly unfulfilling lives in the meantime).<br /> <br /> That's the height of DB success in 3E; I'm not quite impressed by their prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> <br /> \u201cNext to Eshuvar, Kingfisher Swift leaned heavily <br /> on her mace, her unit\u2019s standard propped beside <br /> her. Her legion\u2019s talon had made up the bulk of the <br /> Hunt\u2019s forces\u201d<br /> <br /> A talon is 125 soldiers, so more than that. All we know is that they all died or fled, and the Immaculate commander died. Then 5 DBs went back in and fucking wrecked the Lunars in their home turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:25:27-08:00","id":1295106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295091#post1295091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The height of Dragon Blooded success in Third Edition is the Realm. Broken down then into the kinds of feats ascribed to the Great Houses, such as Ragara's secret experiments, or Ledaal arming itself for war against the Deathlords, or Peleps being so huge that they could plausibly break off and turn the West into their own separate empire with blackjack and hookers. Further devolved into the innumerable feats ascribed to individual sample characters in the House write-ups and Artifact backstories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like that about the book, each individual house is more powerful than any non-Realm nation in the world. You could make House Cathak the main villain of your chronicle and still have it be epic. If they went absolutely full hog, which admittedly they never would do because it\u2019s a tactically stupid decision, they could easily bring 50,000 soldiers and 1,000 Dragonblooded to bear in a conflict.<br /> <br /> Which again is not something any ST should really ever do because there\u2019s no way that would happen. But like, it theoretically could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:32:03-08:00","id":1295107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295106#post1295106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually really like that about the book, each individual house is more powerful than any non-Realm nation in the world. You could make House Cathak the main villain of your chronicle and still have it be epic. If they went absolutely full hog, which admittedly they never would do because it\u2019s a tactically stupid decision, they could easily bring 50,000 soldiers and 1,000 Dragonblooded to bear in a conflict.<br /> <br /> Which again is not something any ST should really ever do because there\u2019s no way that would happen. But like, it theoretically could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not easily because as you said it would be tactically stupid. Your house respects you less if you drain your resources pointless at a time when debt collectors are hounding everyone.<br /> <br /> And Lookshy, Thorns, The Skullstone Archipelago and Prasad would definitely oppose the notion that House Ledaal or dying Tepet, endangered Iselsi or even Okay Sesus could take them one one one.<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> But I get your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T13:09:46-08:00","id":1295116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295107#post1295107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well not easily because as you said it would be tactically stupid. Your house respects you less if you drain your resources pointless at a time when debt collectors are hounding everyone.<br /> <br /> And Lookshy, Thorns, The Skullstone Archipelago and Prasad would definitely oppose the notion that House Ledaal or dying Tepet, endangered Iselsi or even Okay Sesus could take them one one one.<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> But I get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if they withdrew from all of their holdings they\u2019d lose them all pretty quickly, the rest of the Realm would both lose respect for them and take advantage of the situation to take everything ELSE that they had, and in less than a year the great house would be no more. But like, almost any other nation could sacrifice literally everything, conscript every citizen into the army, drain the coffers, and still not be anywhere near powerful enough to destroy Thorns. House Cathak actually probably could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T15:41:29-08:00","id":1295139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295082#post1295082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to understand an unknown number of people as at least 100 soldiers, though I'm not sure why. Further, they 5v2 (after having several DBs killed) kill one and capture the other... who later escapes (after we find the most of the five have lived fairly unfulfilling lives in the meantime).<br /> <br /> That's the height of DB success in 3E; I'm not quite impressed by their prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that someone else screwed up and let them escape after the 5 of them took on 2 celestials and won so handily they had the luxury of taking 1 alive (and successfully brought them back to Big Red) is hardly relevant to their accomplishment. And as you said, we don't know how many other people were in the Wyld Hunt (including how many dragon blooded) so its hard to say how bad of a loss it was. The story also, however, makes it clear they went in cocky instead of playing it smart and got humbled for it as part of the reason why they lost. They didn't even bother making a sworn brotherhood and they recklessly charged ahead instead of waiting for the full Hunt to be assembled (it confirmed more forces were on their way but they didn't wait for them) so that speaks pretty damn ill of the tactical skill their 'vaunted' up and comer leader was bringing to the game. So arguably the only thing the massacres an example of is what happens when you put an arrogant 'rising star' with their head up their ass in charge of a hunt instead of what a well run one looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T16:40:14-08:00","id":1295149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1294421-how-does-the-wild-hunt-ever-corner-lunars?p=1295139#post1295139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So arguably the only thing the massacres an example of is what happens when you put an arrogant 'rising star' with their head up their ass in charge of a hunt instead of what a well run one looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had more time on my hands I'd write a short story about a Shahan-ya and an elder of the Wyld Hunt who have been battling eachother for centuries, knowing eachothers tricks intricately, each one losing Lunar students or younger hunters in their engagements. Each time though, whoever the victor is, they both escape to fight again, coming to the point where both young Lunars and DBs question seemingly nonsensical moves &quot;Why don't we give chase?&quot; or &quot;Why must we hide here? I don't sense anything.&quot; but it's just because they know eachother so well that they're deftly countering moves before they even happen.<br /> <br /> Until eventually, when the Terrestrial is very old, they corner eachother, coming face to face for the first time in decades, and now they're totally unsure how to proceed. They're well aware of how many friends have died in the struggle, and likewise well aware of how much heartache they have inflicted on one another. The DB knows how well the Lunar liked their last student, the Lunar knows how close the DB was to their younger cousin while they were still alive. They both agree that enough blood has been spilled on their account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}